1
00:00:28,280 --> 00:00:30,280
Okay!

2
00:00:31,260 --> 00:00:34,060
Alright!

3
00:00:33,670 --> 00:00:38,810
Whoa, it's set to voice transmission!

4
00:00:38,410 --> 00:00:47,560
Both are coming through~ It's doubled~

5
00:00:48,470 --> 00:00:53,270
Yesterday I had a chill time with Kanata, but that's not happening today.

6
00:00:53,270 --> 00:00:55,270
I can't afford to take it easy.

7
00:00:55,270 --> 00:00:57,270
Seems easy enough, right?

8
00:00:57,270 --> 00:00:58,130
I can't take it easy.

9
00:00:58,130 --> 00:01:00,050
I really can't take it easy.

10
00:01:00,050 --> 00:01:04,360
Phew...

11
00:01:04,360 --> 00:01:08,950
Hustle, hustle.

12
00:01:08,950 --> 00:01:13,040
It's been a while since my last stream, so I should give a recap.

13
00:01:13,040 --> 00:01:16,070
So, today we're going hunting for tanks with Luna.

14
00:01:16,070 --> 00:01:17,210
Yep.

15
00:01:17,210 --> 00:01:18,410
Yep, that's it.

16
00:01:18,410 --> 00:01:19,590
That's the recap.

17
00:01:19,590 --> 00:01:21,350
That was the whole thing.

18
00:01:21,350 --> 00:01:23,780
That's a recap?

19
00:01:23,780 --> 00:01:27,460
That's the recap.

20
00:01:28,840 --> 00:01:34,500
Missiles restocked, hazmat suit—

21
00:01:34,500 --> 00:01:37,190
What a mess.

22
00:01:37,190 --> 00:01:41,790
I made a bunch more missile ammo and added it here.

23
00:01:41,790 --> 00:01:44,590
3, 4... 12, I've got 12.

24
00:01:44,590 --> 00:01:47,590
Should I bring more?

25
00:01:47,590 --> 00:01:51,390
I missed quite a bit yesterday. Probably because I had too many.

26
00:01:51,390 --> 00:01:54,190
How many did you miss?

27
00:01:54,190 --> 00:01:57,190
Couldn't hit anything, huh?

28
00:01:57,190 --> 00:01:58,990
Couldn't hit a thing.

29
00:01:58,990 --> 00:02:00,990
More food, more food.

30
00:02:00,990 --> 00:02:05,880
Food's decent enough.

31
00:02:05,880 --> 00:02:07,880
The helmet is just way too weak.

32
00:02:07,880 --> 00:02:09,880
Tank Dismantling Center.

33
00:02:09,880 --> 00:02:14,480
We're dismantling the barracks, so... Tuck Hamburger.

34
00:02:14,480 --> 00:02:20,880
It's turned into such a proper shop, huh.

35
00:02:20,880 --> 00:02:22,880
Haven't I shown you this yet?

36
00:02:22,880 --> 00:02:23,880
Seriously!

37
00:02:23,880 --> 00:02:25,680
It's become a real shop.

38
00:02:25,680 --> 00:02:28,320
We made quite a bit of money with this.

39
00:02:28,320 --> 00:02:34,460
We still have 5000 scrap though.

40
00:02:34,460 --> 00:02:36,060
We still have 5000 scrap?

41
00:02:36,060 --> 00:02:37,380
Yep.

42
00:02:37,380 --> 00:02:38,680
What are we gonna do with that 5000?

43
00:02:38,680 --> 00:02:42,580
Wait, didn't we use a lot yesterday?

44
00:02:42,580 --> 00:02:45,960
Guess we didn't use as much as I thought.

45
00:02:45,960 --> 00:02:48,860
Should we do something with it in the night session?

46
00:02:48,860 --> 00:02:51,900
We'll just have to burn through the 5000 at night.

47
00:02:51,900 --> 00:02:54,780
This 5000...

48
00:02:54,780 --> 00:02:56,600
What a waste.

49
00:02:56,600 --> 00:02:59,280
It's actually gone up somehow.

50
00:02:59,280 --> 00:03:00,680
Sorry, I ended up increasing it.

51
00:03:00,680 --> 00:03:02,100
Yeah, I did kind of increase it.

52
00:03:02,100 --> 00:03:05,000
We've got materials to spare.

53
00:03:05,000 --> 00:03:07,520
Before you know it, Polka's just...

54
00:03:07,520 --> 00:03:10,400
hoarding scrap...

55
00:03:10,400 --> 00:03:11,520
like some kind of demon.

56
00:03:11,520 --> 00:03:14,420
How much are you gonna stockpile?

57
00:03:14,420 --> 00:03:16,280
We'd all have to...

58
00:03:16,280 --> 00:03:18,900
like, practice with the big helicopter,

59
00:03:18,900 --> 00:03:23,800
or basically just be riding the big heli nonstop — otherwise there's no way to spend it all.

60
00:03:23,800 --> 00:03:27,200
As far as ways to spend the money go—

61
00:03:27,200 --> 00:03:28,880
You can't buy a tank, can you?

62
00:03:28,880 --> 00:03:30,680
Buy a tank.

63
00:03:30,680 --> 00:03:32,040
Can you actually buy one?

64
00:03:32,040 --> 00:03:34,620
Buying a tank would be hilarious.

65
00:03:34,620 --> 00:03:35,980
That idea...

66
00:03:35,980 --> 00:03:41,570
is something else.

67
00:03:41,570 --> 00:03:42,930
A b-boat!

68
00:03:42,930 --> 00:03:45,850
Alright, a boat, a boat!

69
00:03:45,850 --> 00:03:48,570
A boat, wait—

70
00:03:48,570 --> 00:03:50,370
Might as well make one.

71
00:03:50,370 --> 00:03:51,210
There we go.

72
00:03:51,210 --> 00:03:53,050
Take that, boat!

73
00:03:53,050 --> 00:03:55,510
Okay, and...

74
00:03:55,510 --> 00:03:56,570
Alright.

75
00:03:56,570 --> 00:03:58,950
It turned to night!

76
00:03:58,950 --> 00:04:00,110
It's night now.

77
00:04:00,110 --> 00:04:00,950
Is this morning?

78
00:04:00,950 --> 00:04:01,610
Or night?

79
00:04:01,610 --> 00:04:03,770
Wait, is it turning to night?

80
00:04:03,770 --> 00:04:09,930
It's going to be night.

81
00:04:09,930 --> 00:04:11,670
Let's wait until it gets light before we go.

82
00:04:11,670 --> 00:04:12,970
Okay.

83
00:04:12,970 --> 00:04:14,550
Is the camper van okay?

84
00:04:14,550 --> 00:04:15,990
It hasn't decayed, has it?

85
00:04:15,990 --> 00:04:17,350
No decay.

86
00:04:17,350 --> 00:04:17,770
Nice!

87
00:04:17,770 --> 00:04:20,570
One vehicle should be more than enough now, right?

88
00:04:20,570 --> 00:04:25,370
So there's a chance we don't even need to use it?

89
00:04:25,370 --> 00:04:26,270
Exactly.

90
00:04:26,270 --> 00:04:26,770
Hold on.

91
00:04:26,770 --> 00:04:27,670
But still...

92
00:04:27,670 --> 00:04:28,670
Don't underestimate it.

93
00:04:28,670 --> 00:04:29,970
This is Polka we're talking about.

94
00:04:29,970 --> 00:04:34,470
Just because Azukichi taught you a bunch of stuff yesterday doesn't mean...

95
00:04:34,470 --> 00:04:35,870
Okay, fair point.

96
00:04:35,870 --> 00:04:37,470
Yeah, you're kind of getting a little cocky.

97
00:04:37,470 --> 00:04:42,070
A nearly gold bag is sticking out.

98
00:04:45,930 --> 00:04:48,910
No matter how much you've been taught...

99
00:04:48,910 --> 00:04:50,910
Oh, it's glowing!

100
00:04:50,910 --> 00:04:54,380
Gold!

101
00:04:54,380 --> 00:04:58,200
The princess is fine on her own, and now she's the one worrying about us.

102
00:04:58,200 --> 00:04:59,400
That makes no sense.

103
00:04:59,400 --> 00:05:01,660
Normally there'd be someone protecting the princess...

104
00:05:01,660 --> 00:05:03,460
But the princess is fine on her own.

105
00:05:03,460 --> 00:05:05,040
What's going on?

106
00:05:05,040 --> 00:05:07,480
But yesterday she was totally fine, for real.

107
00:05:07,480 --> 00:05:10,480
Polka is really trusted.

108
00:05:10,480 --> 00:05:11,760
The irony.

109
00:05:11,760 --> 00:05:14,700
Seriously, yesterday we were way too close to that tank.

110
00:05:14,700 --> 00:05:18,060
Yeah, that's true — it was right near Kanata's place.

111
00:05:18,060 --> 00:05:20,860
Right, apparently it's better if it's not that close.

112
00:05:20,860 --> 00:05:22,040
Yeah, yeah, yeah.

113
00:05:22,040 --> 00:05:23,700
Hmm.

114
00:05:23,700 --> 00:05:24,560
Hmm.

115
00:05:24,560 --> 00:05:29,750
If something good drops today...

116
00:05:29,750 --> 00:05:30,650
That'd be a win.

117
00:05:30,650 --> 00:05:32,250
Well, if we destroy the tank, that's a win.

118
00:05:32,250 --> 00:05:34,810
Oh, like...

119
00:05:34,810 --> 00:05:36,410
The items...

120
00:05:36,410 --> 00:05:42,510
The rare drops are like, something starting with N or M...

121
00:05:43,410 --> 00:05:45,770
It's gotta be the M249. The M249.

122
00:05:45,770 --> 00:05:48,010
M249 something.

123
00:05:48,010 --> 00:05:49,590
The M249 can drop from it.

124
00:05:49,590 --> 00:05:51,610
And it still hasn't dropped yet.

125
00:05:51,610 --> 00:05:54,910
It's probably Kanatan's dream too.

126
00:05:54,910 --> 00:05:56,510
Oh right, it really hasn't dropped.

127
00:05:56,510 --> 00:05:59,810
Yeah, the M249...

128
00:05:59,810 --> 00:06:01,190
Kanatan's always been saying

129
00:06:01,190 --> 00:06:04,470
"I want it!"

130
00:06:04,470 --> 00:06:06,150
The L96 has dropped though.

131
00:06:06,150 --> 00:06:08,750
Yeah, the black one dropped.

132
00:06:08,750 --> 00:06:10,370
So we're going for the M249.

133
00:06:10,370 --> 00:06:12,990
If the M249 drops, we'll probably finally feel at peace.

134
00:06:12,990 --> 00:06:14,490
We'll finally be at peace.

135
00:06:14,490 --> 00:06:14,990
Hmm.

136
00:06:14,990 --> 00:06:17,230
Everyone will finally be at peace.

137
00:06:17,230 --> 00:06:17,730
Hmm.

138
00:06:17,730 --> 00:06:22,990
And then we prove just how powerful it is.

139
00:06:22,990 --> 00:06:25,890
Will it drop? Will it drop?

140
00:06:25,890 --> 00:06:27,150
I'm gonna eat this.

141
00:06:27,150 --> 00:06:29,350
Tasty.

142
00:06:29,350 --> 00:06:32,990
Yesterday I was totally freaking out, but...

143
00:06:32,990 --> 00:06:36,420
Now I feel totally relaxed.

144
00:06:36,420 --> 00:06:38,100
Wait, is that a flag?

145
00:06:38,100 --> 00:06:39,400
We've got this in the bag.

146
00:06:39,400 --> 00:06:41,040
D-do it!

147
00:06:41,040 --> 00:06:42,000
We've got this in the bag.

148
00:06:42,000 --> 00:06:45,600
Do it! Do the Easter egg hunt!

149
00:06:45,600 --> 00:06:46,200
Huh!?

150
00:06:46,200 --> 00:06:49,100
But there's a helicopter flying around.

151
00:06:49,100 --> 00:06:50,300
Yeah, that's... that's scary.

152
00:06:50,300 --> 00:06:54,470
Live without a bunny or a basket.

153
00:06:54,470 --> 00:06:56,370
There's a helicopter out there.

154
00:06:56,370 --> 00:06:58,370
It's there.

155
00:06:58,370 --> 00:07:01,460
And I can hear animal sounds nearby too.

156
00:07:01,460 --> 00:07:04,360
Pumpkin~ pumpkin~

157
00:07:04,360 --> 00:07:05,660
Yummy~ yummy~

158
00:07:05,660 --> 00:07:06,780
Huh? Nobody's here?

159
00:07:06,780 --> 00:07:08,380
No pumpkins~

160
00:07:08,380 --> 00:07:12,040
Oh, oh, pumpkin~

161
00:07:12,040 --> 00:07:14,640
There should be some around here though.

162
00:07:14,640 --> 00:07:15,440
Ha!

163
00:07:15,440 --> 00:07:16,440
Ha!

164
00:07:16,440 --> 00:07:18,860
Ha!

165
00:07:18,860 --> 00:07:20,360
One!

166
00:07:20,360 --> 00:07:21,460
Got one~

167
00:07:21,460 --> 00:07:23,160
If we're gonna go for a one-two combo—

168
00:07:23,160 --> 00:07:24,760
Hmm...

169
00:07:24,760 --> 00:07:26,160
There are only two of us here.

170
00:07:26,160 --> 00:07:28,860
You can get 3 Silver Eggs from this, right?

171
00:07:28,860 --> 00:07:32,010
Oh, you get 3?

172
00:07:32,010 --> 00:07:34,010
Yeah, when nobody else is around—

173
00:07:34,010 --> 00:07:37,490
If you're in first place, you probably get like 3 Silver Eggs.

174
00:07:37,490 --> 00:07:39,090
Wow, that many?

175
00:07:39,090 --> 00:07:44,170
First place! Can you get first with just one?

176
00:07:44,170 --> 00:07:52,420
Oh, but Polka was slower so she's in second place. By the scoring.

177
00:07:52,420 --> 00:07:54,540
Is there no tied first place?

178
00:07:54,540 --> 00:07:59,910
Hahaha!

179
00:07:59,910 --> 00:08:01,810
It's almost noon now.

180
00:08:01,810 --> 00:08:03,930
Yep, it's noon.

181
00:08:03,930 --> 00:08:04,370
So like—

182
00:08:04,370 --> 00:08:05,730
When the cannon comes—

183
00:08:05,730 --> 00:08:07,310
You do the crab walk.

184
00:08:07,310 --> 00:08:07,810
Hm?

185
00:08:07,810 --> 00:08:09,550
Wait, tell me about that.

186
00:08:09,550 --> 00:08:12,210
The crab walk.

187
00:08:12,210 --> 00:08:12,510
Yeah.

188
00:08:12,510 --> 00:08:13,610
The cannon—

189
00:08:13,610 --> 00:08:15,170
When the cannon fires—

190
00:08:15,170 --> 00:08:16,530
It goes bam bam bam bam—

191
00:08:16,530 --> 00:08:17,630
You get shot, right?

192
00:08:17,630 --> 00:08:18,890
Yeah yeah yeah.

193
00:08:18,890 --> 00:08:20,510
When the cannon comes—

194
00:08:20,510 --> 00:08:22,090
You move in one direction—

195
00:08:22,090 --> 00:08:23,950
Tap tap tap tap tap tap—

196
00:08:23,950 --> 00:08:25,410
You do the crab walk like that—

197
00:08:25,410 --> 00:08:26,830
And you can dodge it.

198
00:08:26,830 --> 00:08:28,950
Both of them said the same thing yesterday.

199
00:08:28,950 --> 00:08:29,430
So it really is—

200
00:08:29,430 --> 00:08:33,510
Sideways, huh. Oh yeah yeah yeah, they were doing the same thing.

201
00:08:33,510 --> 00:08:36,930
Pro advice. Taking notes.

202
00:08:36,930 --> 00:08:39,120
Sideways, sideways, sideways.

203
00:08:39,120 --> 00:08:43,390
Like, don't move in both directions — just keep going one way.

204
00:08:43,390 --> 00:08:46,850
Tap tap tap tap tap — do the crab.

205
00:08:46,850 --> 00:08:47,800
Engage with it.

206
00:08:57,650 --> 00:08:59,735
How elegant~

207
00:08:59,735 --> 00:09:01,375
Wait, there's still a bed left?

208
00:09:01,375 --> 00:09:01,915
Over there still—

209
00:09:03,120 --> 00:09:10,655
I'm going camping-style! Let's go! Polka remembers exactly where she died yesterday!

210
00:09:10,655 --> 00:09:15,590
Let's go! Let's go! Yeah, let's head out! I'm going!

211
00:09:15,590 --> 00:09:19,190
Let's gooo! I'm getting pumped! Let's do this!

212
00:09:19,190 --> 00:09:22,790
Okay, are we heading out? Yep.

213
00:09:22,790 --> 00:09:24,790
Oh wait! Should we take two vehicles?

214
00:09:24,790 --> 00:09:27,390
Hm? Two vehicles?

215
00:09:27,390 --> 00:09:30,340
Just in case, let's take two. Two vehicles.

216
00:09:30,340 --> 00:09:33,190
We've got plenty of room though, one is honestly fine.

217
00:09:33,190 --> 00:09:38,790
Ah, fair enough. One's fine then. I'll leave it to you.

218
00:09:38,790 --> 00:09:40,590
Alright.

219
00:09:40,590 --> 00:09:42,590
We're way too comfortable with this.

220
00:09:42,590 --> 00:09:44,670
Yeah, we're way too relaxed.

221
00:09:44,670 --> 00:09:47,430
It'll probably be fine, I'm sure.

222
00:09:47,430 --> 00:09:49,490
Yesterday, even after it ended—

223
00:09:49,490 --> 00:09:51,370
Oh, there was only one.

224
00:09:51,370 --> 00:09:56,450
I bet yesterday she was secretly taking down like 5 or 6 tanks after the event. She'll be fine.

225
00:09:56,450 --> 00:09:58,330
Did the eggs come? Hold on—

226
00:09:58,330 --> 00:10:01,930
Wait, Polka's getting left behind too!

227
00:10:01,930 --> 00:10:02,770
Why are you doing the same thing—

228
00:10:02,770 --> 00:10:04,470
Three came!

229
00:10:04,470 --> 00:10:05,030
Same!

230
00:10:05,030 --> 00:10:06,790
This—

231
00:10:06,790 --> 00:10:10,150
I placed it!

232
00:10:10,150 --> 00:10:13,000
How do you get down from here?

233
00:10:13,000 --> 00:10:14,540
Hm? You can get down with Space, right?

234
00:10:14,540 --> 00:10:18,260
Right? You can get down with Space? Normally?

235
00:10:18,260 --> 00:10:23,010
There's no day where you can't get down with Space, right?

236
00:10:23,010 --> 00:10:26,870
Wait, why can't you get down?

237
00:10:26,870 --> 00:10:34,300
Space just suddenly stopped working.

238
00:10:34,300 --> 00:10:35,680
Heave-ho.

239
00:10:35,680 --> 00:10:36,760
There we go.

240
00:10:36,760 --> 00:10:41,220
The passenger seat... like if I move the car a little more I can get in?

241
00:10:41,220 --> 00:10:43,200
Guess not.

242
00:10:43,200 --> 00:10:47,500
There's no passenger seat option, right?

243
00:10:47,500 --> 00:10:50,460
Wait.

244
00:10:50,460 --> 00:10:53,850
I can't get in.

245
00:10:53,850 --> 00:10:54,950
The "get in" option isn't showing up.

246
00:10:54,950 --> 00:10:56,910
Why though?

247
00:10:56,910 --> 00:11:01,360


248
00:11:01,360 --> 00:11:04,510


249
00:11:04,510 --> 00:11:06,290


250
00:11:06,290 --> 00:11:08,430
Got in!

251
00:11:08,430 --> 00:11:10,170
Looks like the position was off.

252
00:11:10,170 --> 00:11:11,150
Bad timing.

253
00:11:11,150 --> 00:11:13,800
Exactly.

254
00:11:13,800 --> 00:11:19,980
That was close — Polka broke out in a cold sweat there!

255
00:11:19,980 --> 00:11:23,980
You were panicking too since you couldn't get in!

256
00:11:23,980 --> 00:11:31,150
There's a helicopter flying around nearby.

257
00:11:31,150 --> 00:11:36,230
Hey! It's kind of heading this way though.

258
00:11:36,230 --> 00:11:42,070
It's right on the road we need to take — and we're the only ones here.

259
00:11:42,070 --> 00:11:49,130
They're totally targeting us!

260
00:11:49,130 --> 00:11:52,430
Obviously.

261
00:11:52,430 --> 00:11:58,450
I was thinking "now's our chance to take down the helicopter" — but nope, we'd definitely get shot. So we just ignored it.

262
00:11:58,450 --> 00:12:01,610
We just ignored it.

263
00:12:01,730 --> 00:12:02,730
Are we okay?

264
00:12:02,730 --> 00:12:03,730
We're fine.

265
00:12:03,730 --> 00:12:11,470
Oh, some supply drops are falling right above us.

266
00:12:11,470 --> 00:12:14,070
Wait, they're close?

267
00:12:14,070 --> 00:12:16,070
We don't need any more supplies!

268
00:12:16,070 --> 00:12:23,770
It's an indiscriminate attack!

269
00:12:23,770 --> 00:12:29,710
I'm just an innocent civilian!

270
00:12:29,710 --> 00:12:31,510
What is going on?!

271
00:12:32,960 --> 00:12:35,760
A civilian?

272
00:12:35,760 --> 00:12:36,760
Wait, Makkuru?

273
00:12:36,760 --> 00:12:37,760
Wait, it just keeps—

274
00:12:37,760 --> 00:12:43,410
Are you kidding me?!

275
00:12:43,410 --> 00:12:46,300
Hey, stop with the serious stuff!

276
00:12:46,300 --> 00:12:49,100
Missiles?! Are you serious?!

277
00:12:49,100 --> 00:12:51,900
Hey, don't you dare fly off looking all satisfied!

278
00:12:51,900 --> 00:12:55,700
Hey, right now—

