No way!

559
00:25:55,170 --> 00:25:56,970
To think it would come to this...

560
00:25:56,970 --> 00:26:01,360
Who could have foreseen this...

561
00:26:01,360 --> 00:26:02,160
N-no way...

562
00:26:02,160 --> 00:26:04,160
This plan is falling apart way too hard.

563
00:26:04,160 --> 00:26:13,160
It's not like they're just wandering around the perimeter anymore.

564
00:26:13,960 --> 00:26:16,880
I can't hear anything though.

565
00:26:16,880 --> 00:26:21,490
Thanks for telling me about the rooftop area.

566
00:26:21,490 --> 00:26:23,990
Huh? It's not that high though.

567
00:26:23,990 --> 00:26:31,010
Hey, stop washing cars around back.

568
00:26:31,010 --> 00:26:34,170
"Back car wash"?

569
00:26:34,170 --> 00:26:35,650
What even is a "back car wash"?

570
00:26:35,650 --> 00:26:38,610
Front coordination, back car wash.

571
00:26:38,610 --> 00:26:39,110
"Front"...

572
00:26:39,110 --> 00:26:42,250
Wait, huh? What?

573
00:26:42,250 --> 00:26:45,310
There's no sound at all.

574
00:26:45,310 --> 00:26:47,410
It's super peaceful.

575
00:26:47,410 --> 00:26:51,710
Too peaceful. What was the point of us getting killed yesterday?

576
00:26:51,710 --> 00:26:53,710
Maybe there were never any tanks here to begin with.

577
00:26:53,710 --> 00:26:55,910
Was it all an illusion?

578
00:26:55,910 --> 00:26:57,610
An illuuusion~

579
00:26:57,610 --> 00:26:59,410
It was~

580
00:26:59,410 --> 00:27:01,510
No way. So when do tanks even spawn?

581
00:27:01,510 --> 00:27:03,110
Spawn now! Come on, spawn already!

582
00:27:03,110 --> 00:27:05,710
Seriously though~

583
00:27:06,810 --> 00:27:09,810
Let me check the rooftop just in case.

584
00:27:09,810 --> 00:27:14,810
Let me scout it out just in case.

585
00:27:14,810 --> 00:27:18,410
Is anyone there?

586
00:27:18,410 --> 00:27:25,550
Has anyone defeated a tank recently?

587
00:27:25,550 --> 00:27:27,410
That sounds kinda artsy and I don't like it.

588
00:27:27,410 --> 00:27:31,210
That came out in a weird way.

589
00:27:31,210 --> 00:27:32,210
The spacing is like...

590
00:27:32,210 --> 00:27:34,210
I thought it'd be easier to read.

591
00:27:36,010 --> 00:27:37,570


592
00:27:37,570 --> 00:27:41,070
"Someone... space... psyche"... like that...

593
00:27:41,070 --> 00:27:43,150


594
00:27:43,150 --> 00:27:44,650
Haah...

595
00:27:44,650 --> 00:27:46,250
Ugh... production lingo...

596
00:27:46,250 --> 00:27:49,850
We really should've reserved the tank in advance! Are you serious?!

597
00:27:49,850 --> 00:27:50,810
That's scary!

598
00:27:50,810 --> 00:27:52,810
No one's gonna do it now!

599
00:27:52,810 --> 00:27:56,850
I knew everyone would rush to the tank on the last day! Polka called it!

600
00:27:56,850 --> 00:27:58,650
Stop last-minute rushing the tank!

601
00:27:58,650 --> 00:28:02,250
I totally knew the tank would become the hottest content today!

602
00:28:02,250 --> 00:28:05,010
Why?! I guess we should've written down all the tank time slots...

603
00:28:05,010 --> 00:28:06,810
and kept track of them.

604
00:28:06,810 --> 00:28:07,410
Reservations.

605
00:28:07,410 --> 00:28:10,890
We needed hourly reservations for this.

606
00:28:10,890 --> 00:28:11,730
Exactly.

607
00:28:11,730 --> 00:28:13,090
Like, which hour's tank slot is...

608
00:28:13,090 --> 00:28:15,670
Shouldn't we have written it out like a Pol-Luna schedule or something?

609
00:28:15,670 --> 00:28:18,130
Are you serious?

610
00:28:18,130 --> 00:28:19,350
It's over.

611
00:28:19,350 --> 00:28:21,930
No way.

612
00:28:21,930 --> 00:28:23,170
It's over, Luna-san.

613
00:28:23,170 --> 00:28:23,730
The tank...

614
00:28:23,730 --> 00:28:24,290
is gone.

615
00:28:24,290 --> 00:28:25,290
Tank extermination quest...

616
00:28:25,290 --> 00:28:27,270
Tank...

617
00:28:27,270 --> 00:28:31,130
Are you serious?

618
00:28:31,130 --> 00:28:32,670
It's not there.

619
00:28:32,670 --> 00:28:39,850
Was it reservation-only?

620
00:28:39,850 --> 00:28:43,130
If we wait, will it respawn?

621
00:28:43,130 --> 00:28:48,970
There was no explosion marker, so it must've been before that.

622
00:28:48,970 --> 00:28:51,710
It probably got scrapped and despawned.

623
00:28:51,710 --> 00:28:56,850
Even if it despawned after being scrapped, it depends on how long ago that was.

624
00:28:56,850 --> 00:28:59,190
How long ago was it, I wonder?

625
00:28:59,190 --> 00:29:01,650
That's why I asked — I wanted to know the time.

626
00:29:01,650 --> 00:29:04,750
Maybe there's nobody left at all?

627
00:29:04,750 --> 00:29:05,870
One tank per hour?

628
00:29:05,870 --> 00:29:07,790
So if it's one tank per hour...

629
00:29:07,790 --> 00:29:11,920
let's hope it was an hour ago.

630
00:29:11,920 --> 00:29:12,620
Will it spawn?

631
00:29:12,620 --> 00:29:16,680
Will it spawn, you think?

632
00:29:16,680 --> 00:29:17,980
If it was an hour ago, then yeah.

633
00:29:17,980 --> 00:29:24,030
How long has it been, I wonder?

634
00:29:31,070 --> 00:29:34,690
Because ever since I logged in...

635
00:29:34,690 --> 00:29:37,740
Peko and Ran didn't have the marker either.

636
00:29:37,740 --> 00:29:45,070
Oh really? I wasn't looking at the map.

637
00:29:45,070 --> 00:29:47,870
16...

638
00:29:47,870 --> 00:29:49,840
Hmm...

639
00:29:49,840 --> 00:29:51,490
I see.

640
00:29:51,490 --> 00:29:53,270
4 PM?

641
00:29:53,270 --> 00:29:55,070
Yeah, around 4:30.

642
00:29:55,070 --> 00:30:01,260
When I checked, it was already fine by then.

643
00:30:01,260 --> 00:30:08,460
So it must have happened before that.

644
00:30:08,460 --> 00:30:13,240
Still...

645
00:30:13,240 --> 00:30:18,830
Should we wait?

646
00:30:18,830 --> 00:30:20,550
I guess we'll wait.

647
00:30:20,550 --> 00:30:24,130
Will it even spawn if we just wait here?

648
00:30:24,130 --> 00:30:25,930
Who knows.

649
00:30:25,930 --> 00:30:27,130
Let's line up.

650
00:30:27,130 --> 00:30:31,930
Excuse me, tank? We're next, okay?

651
00:30:31,930 --> 00:30:33,510
Excuse me!

652
00:30:33,510 --> 00:30:40,290
Next, next, next — we're reserving the next tank!

653
00:30:40,290 --> 00:30:42,410
We're going.

654
00:30:42,410 --> 00:30:43,670
Reservation.

655
00:30:43,670 --> 00:30:46,830
We're in the reservation queue.

656
00:30:46,830 --> 00:30:48,890
Reserving our spot for the next tank.

657
00:30:48,890 --> 00:30:49,870
Go ahead and reserve it!

658
00:30:49,870 --> 00:30:51,710
Reserve it—

659
00:30:51,710 --> 00:30:54,130
Let's reserve it.

660
00:30:54,130 --> 00:30:58,890
I mean, if it's only once an hour, people are gonna...

661
00:30:58,890 --> 00:31:02,010
Yeah, they'll all rush it, huh.

662
00:31:02,010 --> 00:31:08,610
Seems like it. I honestly didn't think there'd be this many people at this hour.

663
00:31:08,610 --> 00:31:13,270
Ugh, I don't have a tank season pass...

664
00:31:13,270 --> 00:31:19,970
The season pass crowd probably wakes up every morning like, "Time for tanks."

665
00:31:19,970 --> 00:31:22,570
I thought we could just go right away.

666
00:31:22,570 --> 00:31:26,190
Same — but those people, like...

667
00:31:26,190 --> 00:31:27,910
Are they even keeping up with it all?

668
00:31:27,910 --> 00:31:31,850
Or do they just enjoy the act of farming?

669
00:31:31,850 --> 00:31:33,950
Honestly, no idea.

670
00:31:33,950 --> 00:31:36,390
There's no way they're using all of it.

671
00:31:36,390 --> 00:31:38,550
Does everyone really want to do tanks that badly?

672
00:31:38,550 --> 00:31:41,350
I heard tanks give the best loot, though.

673
00:31:41,350 --> 00:31:42,310
Oh really?

674
00:31:42,310 --> 00:31:45,470
How was it actually? Did you get good stuff yesterday?

675
00:31:45,470 --> 00:31:48,470
Mmm... well... yeah, I guess.

676
00:31:48,470 --> 00:31:49,770
Hmm?

677
00:31:49,770 --> 00:31:51,260
Was it worth it?

678
00:31:51,260 --> 00:31:54,070
No rare drops, so... I'm not sure.

679
00:31:54,070 --> 00:31:56,870
Do rocket launcher ammo drop from it?

680
00:31:56,870 --> 00:31:59,870
Oh yeah, yeah! Ammo did drop — rocket launcher ammo.

681
00:31:59,870 --> 00:32:03,870
So it drops rocket launcher ammo so you can use it to blow up the next tank?

682
00:32:03,870 --> 00:32:06,670
It's an endless cycle.

683
00:32:06,670 --> 00:32:07,170
Right.

684
00:32:07,170 --> 00:32:10,470
That's why — that's why people can't stop farming it.

685
00:32:11,270 --> 00:32:15,310
I see. I kind of regret not reserving earlier.

686
00:32:15,310 --> 00:32:16,930
But we did reserve this time, so it's fine.

687
00:32:16,930 --> 00:32:19,110
People just joining won't have any context for this, I guarantee it.

688
00:32:19,110 --> 00:32:24,770
Like, why are we still farming at this point?

689
00:32:24,770 --> 00:32:25,990
No no no no no—

690
00:32:25,990 --> 00:32:27,830
It's because it's today, that's why!

691
00:32:27,830 --> 00:32:29,410
Huh?

692
00:32:29,410 --> 00:32:32,090
People might come specifically because it's today!

693
00:32:32,090 --> 00:32:34,890
Ahh, like endlessly pulling a gacha.

694
00:32:34,890 --> 00:32:38,610
Exactly — and today's the last day, so tons of people want to experience the final tank.

695
00:32:38,610 --> 00:32:40,210
Mass farming.

696
00:32:40,210 --> 00:32:42,610
Today is, after all, the last day of PvE.

697
00:32:42,610 --> 00:32:44,450
One last time.

698
00:32:44,450 --> 00:32:48,010
Everyone wants to do a farewell tank run, I think.

699
00:32:48,010 --> 00:32:49,310
That's fair.

700
00:32:49,310 --> 00:32:50,710
A commemorative tank run.

701
00:32:50,710 --> 00:32:53,870
They want to do a commemorative tank farm.

702
00:32:53,870 --> 00:32:54,710
Exactly.

703
00:32:54,710 --> 00:32:58,790
For those just joining — to explain:

704
00:32:58,790 --> 00:33:00,770
We came here to take down a tank,

705
00:33:00,770 --> 00:33:03,270
but there was no tank.

706
00:33:03,270 --> 00:33:06,580
So for now—

707
00:33:06,580 --> 00:33:08,760
We can watch, at least.

708
00:33:08,760 --> 00:33:11,100
We don't really know where it roams either.

709
00:33:11,100 --> 00:33:12,180
No idea.

710
00:33:12,180 --> 00:33:13,620
Well, I didn't even go inside earlier.

711
00:33:13,620 --> 00:33:15,970
Yeah, I was shooting from way outside just now.

712
00:33:15,970 --> 00:33:17,140
Right, like...

713
00:33:17,140 --> 00:33:20,240
I think Azukichi was told to fight it from a distance.

714
00:33:20,240 --> 00:33:22,780
Something like that, I think.

715
00:33:22,780 --> 00:33:24,100
Yeah, yeah, exactly.

716
00:33:24,100 --> 00:33:27,810
So, chances to encounter the tank...

717
00:33:27,810 --> 00:33:29,550
If it's once an hour...

718
00:33:29,550 --> 00:33:31,070
About 8 more times.

719
00:33:31,070 --> 00:33:32,390
"About 8 more times" — that's kind of funny.

720
00:33:32,390 --> 00:33:35,360
All the tank slots might already be reserved.

721
00:33:35,360 --> 00:33:36,750
Yeah, 8 times is a lot.

722
00:33:36,750 --> 00:33:38,230
First come, first served.

723
00:33:38,230 --> 00:33:39,990
There might be someone out there

724
00:33:39,990 --> 00:33:41,850
who's dead set on taking out every single tank.

725
00:33:41,850 --> 00:33:44,150
Someone who's like "I'm doing ALL of them!"

726
00:33:44,150 --> 00:33:45,550
I wonder if there is.

727
00:33:45,550 --> 00:33:46,870
First come, first served.

728
00:33:46,870 --> 00:33:48,430
Around 4 o'clock, you think?

729
00:33:48,430 --> 00:33:50,110
I think it spawns at 4.

730
00:33:50,110 --> 00:33:53,550
Who took it down and when?

731
00:33:53,550 --> 00:33:57,130
When Uchu logged in.

732
00:33:57,130 --> 00:33:58,410
Wait, no—

733
00:33:58,410 --> 00:34:00,230
Was it after it was already done?

734
00:34:00,230 --> 00:34:02,510
Yeah, it was already finished by then.

735
00:34:02,510 --> 00:34:06,110
When Polka checked the map,

736
00:34:06,110 --> 00:34:07,650
it was already gone.

737
00:34:07,650 --> 00:34:11,230
Maybe it'll spawn again soon?

738
00:34:11,230 --> 00:34:16,970
Yeah, I'm hoping so.

739
00:34:16,970 --> 00:34:20,370
Yesterday we were shooting from around here.

740
00:34:20,370 --> 00:34:22,650
Ah, I see.

741
00:34:22,650 --> 00:34:24,130
So this area works too.

742
00:34:24,130 --> 00:34:25,770
Bullets flying by — whoosh whoosh!

743
00:34:25,770 --> 00:34:28,230
They were stacked over there.

744
00:34:28,230 --> 00:34:30,770
Around NE50.

745
00:34:30,770 --> 00:34:32,330
They stack up too?

746
00:34:32,330 --> 00:34:35,370
They were totally stacked and not moving at all,

747
00:34:35,370 --> 00:34:38,290
so that's where I was aiming.

748
00:34:38,290 --> 00:34:39,830
Stack up already!

749
00:34:39,830 --> 00:34:42,670
Oh, does an announcement pop up when it spawns?

750
00:34:42,670 --> 00:34:43,990


751
00:34:43,990 --> 00:34:47,630
Oh right, it does — that red notification.

752
00:34:47,630 --> 00:34:49,830
Something like "[X] has respawned."

753
00:34:49,830 --> 00:34:51,170
What does the tank show up as in the notification?

754
00:34:51,170 --> 00:34:52,570
Like "CH" something?

755
00:34:52,570 --> 00:34:54,250
It shows up as "CH something," right?

756
00:34:54,250 --> 00:34:56,830
I wonder if it just says "tank."

757
00:34:56,830 --> 00:34:59,720
I don't know.

758
00:34:59,720 --> 00:35:01,980
The ones I always see—

759
00:35:01,980 --> 00:35:03,700
There's one I can never figure out.

760
00:35:03,700 --> 00:35:06,440
There's the Cargo Ship,

761
00:35:06,440 --> 00:35:11,660
wait, is Cargo Ship the tank?

762
00:35:11,660 --> 00:35:14,120
Hmm, I'm not sure.

763
00:35:14,120 --> 00:35:16,000
It does kind of sound like a tank, doesn't it.

764
00:35:16,000 --> 00:35:18,720
CH is the attack helicopter.

765
00:35:18,720 --> 00:35:21,500
Oh, so the tank doesn't get an announcement?

766
00:35:21,500 --> 00:35:23,080
Cargo Ship is the ship.

767
00:35:23,080 --> 00:35:25,280
Right, "ship" is the ship.

768
00:35:25,280 --> 00:35:27,600
Tank online!

769
00:35:27,600 --> 00:35:29,660
Today the tank came online too.

770
00:35:29,660 --> 00:35:30,380
Make an announcement!

771
00:35:30,380 --> 00:35:33,180
Please bring the tank online!

772
00:35:33,180 --> 00:35:34,800
Spawn us a tank!

773
00:35:34,800 --> 00:35:37,260
That's asking a lot.

774
00:35:37,260 --> 00:35:40,740
I need a tank right now!

775
00:35:40,740 --> 00:35:41,800
Please give us a tank!

776
00:35:41,800 --> 00:35:42,520
Sure, no problem!

777
00:35:42,520 --> 00:35:44,320
Spawn like two of them, please!

778
00:35:44,320 --> 00:35:46,600
Sure thing!

779
00:35:46,600 --> 00:35:49,990
Bold of you.

780
00:35:49,990 --> 00:35:53,070
If the tank logs in too, make a proper announcement for it!

781
00:35:53,070 --> 00:35:56,860
I wonder if it will.

782
00:35:56,860 --> 00:36:02,540
Guess we just have to wait until exactly 4 o'clock.

783
00:36:02,540 --> 00:36:05,440
In the meantime, some light conversation—

784
00:36:05,440 --> 00:36:07,500
So, looking back at the end — how was it?

785
00:36:07,500 --> 00:36:10,960
It went by so fast.

786
00:36:10,960 --> 00:36:13,940
Luna even rearranged her work schedule

787
00:36:13,940 --> 00:36:17,720
to make time for this whole period.

788
00:36:17,720 --> 00:36:20,360
At the start,

789
00:36:20,360 --> 00:36:25,840
I wasn't sure if we could build a working farm in a week,

790
00:36:25,840 --> 00:36:29,600
but it went pretty smoothly overall.

791
00:36:29,600 --> 00:36:35,820
And in the second half, Polka helped out too —

792
00:36:35,820 --> 00:36:36,380
thank you so much!

793
00:36:36,380 --> 00:36:39,700
We also got a huge haul of pumpkins.

794
00:36:39,700 --> 00:36:46,140
I never thought I'd end up taking care of pumpkins myself.

795
00:36:46,140 --> 00:36:48,040
Right?!

796
00:36:48,040 --> 00:36:50,620
We worked on it together.

797
00:36:50,620 --> 00:36:54,060
She's going into her closing remarks.

798
00:36:54,060 --> 00:36:56,320


799
00:36:56,320 --> 00:37:03,420
Calling dibs on the closing! The closing! The closing... closing... closing remarks... Were you trying to do the closing first?

800
00:37:03,420 --> 00:37:09,980
Things are a bit out of order today, huh — like, let's just do the closing now...

801
00:37:09,980 --> 00:37:15,740
Starting with the closing remarks... what kind of stream starts with the closing? Ufufu...

802
00:37:15,740 --> 00:37:18,740
Tanks? Is there anything else interesting here?

803
00:37:18,740 --> 00:37:21,040
Hmm... nope.

804
00:37:21,040 --> 00:37:22,340
Scrap...

805
00:37:22,340 --> 00:37:23,140
Um...

806
00:37:23,140 --> 00:37:26,940
I touched the recycler and stuff,

807
00:37:26,940 --> 00:37:29,940
but I want something more interesting to do here.

808
00:37:29,940 --> 00:37:32,740
There's nothing here.

809
00:37:32,740 --> 00:37:35,460
It's going to be nighttime soon, you know?

810
00:37:35,460 --> 00:37:37,340
Night is lonely.

811
00:37:37,340 --> 00:37:40,220
It's cold, it's dark, you can't see anything.

812
00:37:40,220 --> 00:37:43,140
We'll have no choice but to go back to the camper van.

813
00:37:43,440 --> 00:37:45,240
Then let's go to the camper van.

814
00:37:45,240 --> 00:37:46,560
Let's camp!

815
00:37:46,560 --> 00:37:48,180
Should we shoot down the heli?

816
00:37:48,180 --> 00:37:52,840
Can we do that, big bro?

817
00:37:52,840 --> 00:37:56,500
I don't really know how to deal with the heli either.

818
00:37:56,500 --> 00:38:02,060
If you picked up meat, cook it in the camper van!

819
00:38:02,060 --> 00:38:03,500
Oh, right, meat.

820
00:38:03,500 --> 00:38:06,580
But I don't have any wood.

821
00:38:06,580 --> 00:38:07,980
I brought wood!

822
00:38:07,980 --> 00:38:10,800
Then cook the meat, cook it!

823
00:38:10,800 --> 00:38:12,800
Can you cook in a camper van?

824
00:38:12,800 --> 00:38:14,800
The camper van is hard to get out of — oh, it opened.

825
00:38:14,800 --> 00:38:16,600
Where did we park the car again?

826
00:38:16,600 --> 00:38:17,520
Over there.

827
00:38:17,520 --> 00:38:18,400
Over there.

828
00:38:18,400 --> 00:38:21,200
It's the camper van, found it!

829
00:38:21,200 --> 00:38:25,800
Let's camp out here for a bit.

830
00:38:25,800 --> 00:38:31,600
Can you cook here?

831
00:38:31,600 --> 00:38:32,600
Oh, you can!

832
00:38:32,600 --> 00:38:38,110
Wood.

833
00:38:39,910 --> 00:38:42,980
Can you cook?

834
00:38:42,980 --> 00:38:44,320
Oh, it's cooking!

835
00:38:44,320 --> 00:38:47,980
Isn't it dangerous to cook inside the car?

836
00:38:47,980 --> 00:38:50,960
That's just what camper vans are for.

837
00:38:50,960 --> 00:38:56,890
You'll get carbon monoxide poisoning.

838
00:38:56,890 --> 00:38:59,550
Open a window, open a window!

839
00:38:59,550 --> 00:39:01,390
Carbon monoxide poisoning!

840
00:39:01,390 --> 00:39:02,930
Open the window!

841
00:39:02,930 --> 00:39:05,170
All windows are sealed shut.

842
00:39:05,170 --> 00:39:09,200
That's actually scary.

843
00:39:09,200 --> 00:39:14,420
Oh, the meat is raw — haven't picked up any cooked meat?

844
00:39:14,420 --> 00:39:16,240
Oh, I didn't bring any meat.

845
00:39:16,240 --> 00:39:16,960
Just regular meat.

846
00:39:16,960 --> 00:39:19,260
Just burning it for no reason.

847
00:39:19,260 --> 00:39:23,240
Oh, you're getting charcoal right now.

848
00:39:23,240 --> 00:39:24,420
Getting charcoal.

849
00:39:24,420 --> 00:39:26,840
Oh, I accidentally threw a grenade.

850
00:39:26,840 --> 00:39:28,520
Wait, why did you throw a grenade?

851
00:39:28,520 --> 00:39:29,300
That's scary!

852
00:39:29,300 --> 00:39:31,240
Hey, stop it!

853
00:39:31,240 --> 00:39:34,780
Please don't throw grenades inside the car!

854
00:39:34,780 --> 00:39:36,860
I thought it was going to explode.

855
00:39:38,060 --> 00:39:40,740
Please, stop!

856
00:39:40,740 --> 00:39:44,630
This is way too peaceful, I really don't get it.

857
00:39:45,260 --> 00:39:55,260
I wonder if the in-game time even lines up with real time — oh, you startled me!

858
00:39:55,640 --> 00:40:03,410
Wait, that was just a car outside in real life. Okay, that's done.

859
00:40:03,400 --> 00:40:12,770
Tanks spawning around Polka's place too. Yep, one spawned near me too.

860
00:40:12,770 --> 00:40:19,070
It's going to be night soon. No no no, not night!

861
00:40:19,070 --> 00:40:23,910
Night is a bit dangerous, so once it's daytime again

862
00:40:23,910 --> 00:40:26,810
we'll go for it. By the way—

863
00:40:26,810 --> 00:40:31,170
Oh, you can see the fire from outside too.

864
00:40:31,170 --> 00:40:34,970
The detail is incredible!

865
00:40:34,970 --> 00:40:37,910
Polka is indoors

866
00:40:37,910 --> 00:40:40,710
making

867
00:40:40,710 --> 00:40:43,510
making charcoal right now.

868
00:40:43,510 --> 00:40:46,310
So, how is it? Hearing any sounds?

869
00:40:46,310 --> 00:40:49,200
I mean, we're literally right in the middle of

870
00:40:49,200 --> 00:40:51,070
the enemy's

871
00:40:51,070 --> 00:40:55,710
home base, so it wouldn't be weird if they spawned any second.

872
00:40:55,710 --> 00:40:59,150
This car could get blown up too.

873
00:40:59,150 --> 00:41:04,920
I don't hear anything at all.

874
00:41:04,920 --> 00:41:11,860
Maybe they haven't respawned yet.

875
00:41:11,860 --> 00:41:14,900
Well, it's still about 5 minutes until 4 o'clock.

876
00:41:14,900 --> 00:41:17,000
The tank is probably being built right now,

877
00:41:17,000 --> 00:41:21,380
hopefully it's being built.

878
00:41:21,380 --> 00:41:28,080
We just can't seem to get a good fight going with the tank.

879
00:41:28,080 --> 00:41:28,940
We've been at this

880
00:41:28,940 --> 00:41:31,400
since yesterday.

881
00:41:31,400 --> 00:41:32,740
Yeah, that's right.

882
00:41:32,740 --> 00:41:36,180
Polka said Luna taught her too,

883
00:41:36,180 --> 00:41:37,780
so I'm looking forward to it.

884
00:41:37,780 --> 00:41:39,100
For real.

885
00:41:39,100 --> 00:41:41,360
But today I think

886
00:41:41,360 --> 00:41:44,040
we'll finally get to see it in action.

887
00:41:44,040 --> 00:41:44,820
It's just that...

888
00:41:44,820 --> 00:41:46,880
the timing hasn't been great.

889
00:41:46,880 --> 00:41:50,220
Oh, did lighting the fire raise the comfort level?

890
00:41:50,220 --> 00:41:51,760
It was at 50% yesterday.

891
00:41:51,760 --> 00:41:52,380
Oh, you're right.

892
00:41:52,380 --> 00:41:54,960
So it's comfortable in here now.

893
00:41:54,960 --> 00:41:55,700
Yeah.

894
00:41:55,700 --> 00:42:02,600
The airdrop came down, but

895
00:42:02,600 --> 00:42:07,800
what about our tank?

896
00:42:07,800 --> 00:42:10,560
The tank dropped too,

897
00:42:10,560 --> 00:42:13,000
it's still spawning in.

898
00:42:13,000 --> 00:42:16,240
I wonder if it just pops in from above like ARK dinosaurs.

899
00:42:16,240 --> 00:42:18,840
Who knows,

900
00:42:18,840 --> 00:42:19,500
with tanks.

901
00:42:19,500 --> 00:42:24,620
We started with a bombing drop yesterday, after all.

902
00:42:24,620 --> 00:42:28,020
Yesterday was crazy.

903
00:42:28,020 --> 00:42:29,420
It was a full-on zombie attack.

904
00:42:29,420 --> 00:42:32,520
That was totally unnecessary.

905
00:42:32,520 --> 00:42:37,930
It's night.

906
00:42:37,930 --> 00:42:39,210
It's nighttime.

907
00:42:39,210 --> 00:42:43,470
Come on, spawn already!

908
00:42:43,470 --> 00:42:50,500
Easter event's here!

909
00:42:52,580 --> 00:42:54,900
Gotta do Easter whenever it shows up.

910
00:42:54,900 --> 00:42:55,400
Oh, it's morning.

911
00:42:55,400 --> 00:42:57,220
Does it spawn here?

912
00:42:57,220 --> 00:42:57,920
It's spawning, it's spawning!

913
00:42:57,920 --> 00:42:58,280
Oh, it does spawn here.

914
00:42:58,280 --> 00:43:02,810
Come on, tank, spawn already!

915
00:43:02,810 --> 00:43:04,590
Seriously!

916
00:43:04,590 --> 00:43:05,490
Eggs spawned.

917
00:43:05,490 --> 00:43:08,450
Wait, isn't this event once per hour?

918
00:43:08,450 --> 00:43:11,590
If so, I was thinking an hour's already passed.

919
00:43:11,590 --> 00:43:15,650
You mean an hour after defeating it?

920
00:43:15,650 --> 00:43:17,310
Oh, the Easter event?

921
00:43:17,310 --> 00:43:19,130
Yeah, Easter is once per hour.

922
00:43:19,130 --> 00:43:20,810
I wonder how Easter works exactly.

923
00:43:20,810 --> 00:43:23,070
If so, an hour has passed.

924
00:43:23,070 --> 00:43:25,610
Timing-wise it's been about an hour, yeah.

925
00:43:25,610 --> 00:43:26,010
Right.

926
00:43:26,010 --> 00:43:30,400
We're right where the tank is,

927
00:43:30,400 --> 00:43:32,600
and if we're doing eggs and the tank suddenly shows up

928
00:43:32,400 --> 00:43:33,880
and just opens fire on us,

929
00:43:33,680 --> 00:43:35,920
that would be the worst.

930
00:43:35,920 --> 00:43:37,180
True.

931
00:43:37,180 --> 00:43:39,100
Whose fault would that even be?

932
00:43:39,100 --> 00:43:42,930
It's not here.

933
00:43:42,930 --> 00:43:47,240
No tank.

934
00:43:47,240 --> 00:43:50,630
Is that a helicopter?

935
00:43:50,630 --> 00:43:53,870
That's not a tank sound.

936
00:43:53,870 --> 00:43:57,690
Why isn't it here?

937
00:43:57,690 --> 00:44:01,630
The tank had a much more aggressive sound to it.

938
00:44:01,630 --> 00:44:03,810
What is that sound?

939
00:44:03,810 --> 00:44:06,950
That's probably just something flying overhead.

940
00:44:06,950 --> 00:44:08,030
Something flying overhead?

941
00:44:08,030 --> 00:44:17,610
The tank sounded like it meant business — even the first time I heard it, I could tell.

942
00:44:17,610 --> 00:44:18,430
Yeah.

943
00:44:18,430 --> 00:44:21,690
Even hearing it for the first time, it had this murderous sound to it.

944
00:44:21,710 --> 00:44:25,450
Should we go look for it again?

945
00:44:25,450 --> 00:44:28,810
But when we came here yesterday, the tank was already here.

946
00:44:28,810 --> 00:44:29,810
It was here, right? Yesterday?

947
00:44:29,810 --> 00:44:30,810
It was, right?

948
00:44:30,810 --> 00:44:31,610
It was dropping stuff.

949
00:44:31,610 --> 00:44:33,420
How did the practice go yesterday?

950
00:44:33,420 --> 00:44:38,310
We were dropping it during practice too.

951
00:44:38,310 --> 00:44:45,490
I mean, this is the tank's patrol route to begin with,

952
00:44:45,490 --> 00:44:47,790
so it'd be weird if it wasn't here.

953
00:44:47,790 --> 00:44:54,480
Exactly.

954
00:44:54,480 --> 00:44:56,350
Hmm...

955
00:44:56,350 --> 00:44:59,780
Is it possible we can't tell unless we move away?

956
00:44:59,780 --> 00:45:01,580
Heheh.

957
00:45:01,580 --> 00:45:02,080
Really?

958
00:45:02,080 --> 00:45:03,580
Like, maybe we can't tell because we're standing right here?

959
00:45:03,580 --> 00:45:07,880
I mean, we keep getting notifications like "spawned" and stuff,

960
00:45:07,880 --> 00:45:10,680
so I don't think that's the case.

961
00:45:10,680 --> 00:45:11,780
Hmm, hard to say...

962
00:45:11,780 --> 00:45:13,780
Ponpon, Unatan, I'm going to the bathroom.

963
00:45:13,780 --> 00:45:15,690
Oh, uh, okay.

964
00:45:15,690 --> 00:45:20,780
lol

965
00:45:21,380 --> 00:45:31,380
So, Polka has to step away for a bit tonight, and since I can't be on during prime time,

966
00:45:32,080 --> 00:45:36,320
that's why it ended up being this time slot. But when I come back tonight—

967
00:45:36,320 --> 00:45:40,990
today as well, the date changes at midnight,

968
00:45:40,990 --> 00:45:45,400
and up until then it's the PVE period,

969
00:45:45,400 --> 00:45:50,960
and apparently the server's pretty empty, so I'm hoping to stream then too!

970
00:45:50,960 --> 00:45:54,090
I think Kanata feels the same way.

971
00:45:54,090 --> 00:45:58,130
So please stick around until the end

972
00:45:58,130 --> 00:46:00,650
and enjoy it with us!

973
00:46:00,650 --> 00:46:07,300
But the tanks aren't respawning, huh.

974
00:46:07,300 --> 00:46:13,880
Polka really ended up relying on Luna a lot this time around.

975
00:46:13,880 --> 00:46:23,880
Probably more than even the staff knows — but in return, it was so much fun. Thank you so much for having me!

976
00:46:27,700 --> 00:46:36,470
I'm not sure what'll happen during the PVP period,

977
00:46:36,470 --> 00:46:44,670
but being able to stay with Luna was so much fun.

978
00:46:48,010 --> 00:46:52,610
When I was alone going "ugh, I have no idea what I'm doing," Luna

979
00:46:52,610 --> 00:46:55,810
invited me saying "wanna live together?"

980
00:46:55,810 --> 00:46:58,410
and I gratefully—

981
00:46:58,410 --> 00:47:00,210
They're here!

982
00:47:00,210 --> 00:47:04,890
Luna's here!

983
00:47:04,890 --> 00:47:06,690
Luna, where are you?!

984
00:47:06,690 --> 00:47:08,690
Come here!

985
00:47:08,690 --> 00:47:10,690
The tank's here!

986
00:47:10,490 --> 00:47:12,490
What's going on?

987
00:47:12,490 --> 00:47:18,490
What's happening?

988
00:47:18,490 --> 00:47:26,490
Luna, the tank's here!

989
00:47:26,490 --> 00:47:28,110
Wait, hold on — what? Did it spawn?

990
00:47:27,900 --> 00:47:28,700
It spawned!

991
00:47:28,700 --> 00:47:32,220
Wait, I'm... I'm dead?

992
00:47:32,220 --> 00:47:33,220
WHAT?!

993
00:47:33,020 --> 00:47:35,020
Huh? Huh? Huh? Huh?

994
00:47:35,020 --> 00:47:40,020
Hey, I didn't even go to the bathroom yet — can you not do this to me right now?

995
00:47:40,020 --> 00:47:42,020
Oh wow, Luna's in the red — wait, what?

996
00:47:42,020 --> 00:47:47,020
Are you kidding me—

997
00:47:47,020 --> 00:47:52,020
Luna! Luna? Luna? Luna, didn't you set a bed here?

998
00:47:52,020 --> 00:47:56,020
Ahhh! Wait, the bathroom — ahhh!

999
00:47:56,020 --> 00:47:59,020
What do I do?! Luna! Ahhh!

1000
00:47:59,020 --> 00:48:01,020


1001
00:48:01,020 --> 00:48:03,520
What am I supposed to do?!

1002
00:48:03,520 --> 00:48:05,020
Why?!

1003
00:48:05,020 --> 00:48:09,520
Huh?

1004
00:48:09,520 --> 00:48:11,520
Why NOW of all times?!

1005
00:48:11,520 --> 00:48:15,520
Huh?

1006
00:48:15,520 --> 00:48:20,520
I wasn't even doing anything!

1007
00:48:20,520 --> 00:48:22,520
And I didn't even do anything either!

1008
00:48:22,520 --> 00:48:28,520
My main character got hit by a missile and died.

1009
00:48:29,020 --> 00:48:33,700
The tank did its job, but... I didn't even hear the tank though.

1010
00:48:33,490 --> 00:48:34,890
Huh, why?

1011
00:48:34,890 --> 00:48:38,590
I didn't hear it... I was just talking about how great it was being with Botan — I mean Luna—

1012
00:48:38,590 --> 00:48:41,550
and how much I appreciated her taking care of me,

1013
00:48:41,550 --> 00:48:44,110
and I hadn't even respawned yet?

1014
00:48:44,110 --> 00:48:46,790
I come back and I'm dead?

1015
00:48:46,790 --> 00:48:49,250
What is going on?

1016
00:48:49,250 --> 00:48:52,450
Tank, seriously, stop ghosting me.

1017
00:48:52,450 --> 00:48:54,550
You were watching my stream, weren't you, tank.

1018
00:48:54,550 --> 00:48:56,610
Stop ghosting.

1019
00:48:56,610 --> 00:49:00,350
There's an airdrop that looks like it landed pretty close by.

1020
00:49:00,350 --> 00:49:03,790
Why am I dead?!

1021
00:49:03,790 --> 00:49:08,570
Can you come? Should we split stuff in the car?

1022
00:49:08,570 --> 00:49:14,050
I haven't registered the car so nothing's showing up.

1023
00:49:14,050 --> 00:49:15,050
Bed.

1024
00:49:15,050 --> 00:49:19,850
What should Polka bring to get there? And where exactly?

1025
00:49:19,850 --> 00:49:23,710
I think there's a sleeping bag placed around J-7.

1026
00:49:23,710 --> 00:49:26,010
J-7?

1027
00:49:26,010 --> 00:49:28,450
Yeah, yeah, that's right.

1028
00:49:28,450 --> 00:49:31,010
Somewhere around the same place as yesterday.

1029
00:49:31,010 --> 00:49:33,870
Oh, it said I could set this as my own bed, so—

1030
00:49:33,870 --> 00:49:34,350
Probably.

1031
00:49:34,350 --> 00:49:37,370
Right now—

1032
00:49:37,370 --> 00:49:37,930
Luna,

1033
00:49:37,930 --> 00:49:40,350
Polka's in the car—

1034
00:49:40,350 --> 00:49:42,310
I set it as your bed — how's that?

1035
00:49:42,310 --> 00:49:44,810
But it's greyed out

1036
00:49:44,810 --> 00:49:46,010
and I can't select it. Why?

1037
00:49:46,010 --> 00:49:47,490
It says "in use."

1038
00:49:47,490 --> 00:49:49,850
I just got out and tried,

1039
00:49:49,850 --> 00:49:50,850
Oh it worked, it worked!

1040
00:49:50,850 --> 00:49:56,450
The clothes are in the top.

1041
00:49:56,450 --> 00:49:58,250
Put it on quick!

1042
00:49:58,250 --> 00:50:02,130
No hazmat suit in here.

1043
00:50:02,130 --> 00:50:03,130
Top, top, top!

1044
00:50:03,130 --> 00:50:04,130
The closet!

1045
00:50:04,130 --> 00:50:05,730
Where?

1046
00:50:05,730 --> 00:50:06,730
Top, top, top!

1047
00:50:06,730 --> 00:50:07,730
Found it!

1048
00:50:07,730 --> 00:50:10,530
I thought I was gonna die!

1049
00:50:10,530 --> 00:50:11,330
You did die!

1050
00:50:11,330 --> 00:50:16,130
Wait, isn't that seriously messed up?

1051
00:50:16,930 --> 00:50:19,850
Attacking someone while they're in the bathroom is the worst!

1052
00:50:19,850 --> 00:50:20,970
Did you eat?

1053
00:50:20,970 --> 00:50:22,630
Did you eat?

1054
00:50:22,630 --> 00:50:24,970
I didn't eat.

1055
00:50:24,970 --> 00:50:28,910
Can you stop attacking people while they're in the bathroom?

1056
00:50:28,910 --> 00:50:30,970
Where were you this whole time?

1057
00:50:30,970 --> 00:50:36,770
Weren't you safe on your end too?

1058
00:50:36,770 --> 00:50:39,090
How did you manage to not come out for so long?

1059
00:50:39,090 --> 00:50:41,630
So suddenly—

1060
00:50:41,630 --> 00:50:44,210
"I'm gonna go to the bathroom real quick" right at the end—

1061
00:50:44,210 --> 00:50:47,230
Going then probably wasn't the best idea.

1062
00:50:47,230 --> 00:50:50,530
I didn't think they'd show up!

1063
00:50:50,530 --> 00:50:53,110
That scared me!

1064
00:50:53,110 --> 00:50:56,190
I'm gonna go grab my stuff—

1065
00:50:56,190 --> 00:51:00,210
Oh, okay! I'll come with you, I'll come with you!

1066
00:51:00,210 --> 00:51:02,850
I wanna go get my stuff back!

1067
00:51:02,850 --> 00:51:04,490
This is the worst.

1068
00:51:04,490 --> 00:51:06,170
That's hilarious.

1069
00:51:06,170 --> 00:51:09,650
That guy knew exactly what he was doing.

1070
00:51:09,650 --> 00:51:11,650
What is even going on?

1071
00:51:11,650 --> 00:51:12,650
Why did they suddenly spawn?

1072
00:51:12,650 --> 00:51:14,650
It's just the timing.

1073
00:51:14,650 --> 00:51:20,270
Where's my stuff?

1074
00:51:20,270 --> 00:51:22,070
The rat isn't healing.

1075
00:51:22,070 --> 00:51:23,070
Oh, I hear something!

1076
00:51:23,070 --> 00:51:27,950
Wait, the rat needs to eat something to recover.

1077
00:51:27,950 --> 00:51:28,750
Okay, okay, okay.

1078
00:51:28,750 --> 00:51:32,820
Hold on, the rat thing is—

1079
00:51:32,820 --> 00:51:33,820
It's making noise!

1080
00:51:33,820 --> 00:51:39,200
There we go.

1081
00:51:39,200 --> 00:51:40,320
Drink some water too?

1082
00:51:40,320 --> 00:51:43,860
I had tea so I should be fine on water.

1083
00:51:43,860 --> 00:51:48,450
Man, seriously, seriously...

1084
00:51:48,450 --> 00:51:48,950
Huh?

1085
00:51:48,950 --> 00:51:49,630
Ugh...

1086
00:51:49,630 --> 00:51:51,950
I missed the moment of total defeat.

1087
00:51:51,950 --> 00:51:55,230
The Lunaitos probably saw it though, right?

1088
00:51:55,230 --> 00:51:57,250
But on the escape side—

1089
00:51:57,250 --> 00:51:59,230
I had the options screen open—

1090
00:51:59,230 --> 00:52:00,690
so it was showing that.

1091
00:52:00,690 --> 00:52:01,350
Ahh...

1092
00:52:01,350 --> 00:52:03,750
So what did it look like on your end?

1093
00:52:03,750 --> 00:52:06,530
Polka was in the middle of a super emotional closing moment too.

1094
00:52:06,530 --> 00:52:07,330
Oh no...

1095
00:52:07,330 --> 00:52:09,130
Apparently just a little bit.

1096
00:52:09,130 --> 00:52:12,930
I should've told you to go somewhere safe.

1097
00:52:12,930 --> 00:52:15,830
I just completely—

1098
00:52:15,830 --> 00:52:18,330
I thought they weren't coming, that they still wouldn't come.

1099
00:52:18,330 --> 00:52:19,730
You'd think they wouldn't come, right?

1100
00:52:19,730 --> 00:52:21,730
Hime, you're in rough shape.

1101
00:52:21,730 --> 00:52:23,730
Didn't you practice yesterday? No way!

1102
00:52:23,730 --> 00:52:25,530
Because the whole time—

1103
00:52:25,530 --> 00:52:27,530
You should've practiced bathroom breaks too!

1104
00:52:27,530 --> 00:52:29,530
You weren't there!

1105
00:52:29,530 --> 00:52:32,830
Seriously, where did you die? Like, where?

1106
00:52:35,920 --> 00:52:37,080
Is Pay-chan here?

1107
00:52:37,080 --> 00:52:40,380
Yeah, I hear something from the north.

1108
00:52:40,380 --> 00:52:43,920
Your body should be around here somewhere.

1109
00:52:43,920 --> 00:52:46,680
Found it! You died here!

1110
00:52:46,680 --> 00:52:51,500
There's a death marker here.

1111
00:52:51,500 --> 00:52:55,180
Nice, does that spot look safe?

1112
00:52:55,180 --> 00:52:56,740
Grab it quick!

1113
00:52:56,740 --> 00:52:58,440
Not hearing much right now.

1114
00:52:58,440 --> 00:53:02,980
It's to the north, but I do hear something.

1115
00:53:02,980 --> 00:53:04,880
Alright, let's fall back for now

1116
00:53:04,880 --> 00:53:06,380
and sort out our inventory.

1117
00:53:06,380 --> 00:53:07,980
It's moving away.

1118
00:53:07,980 --> 00:53:09,680
But it's definitely coming from this direction.

1119
00:53:09,680 --> 00:53:10,680
The direction, yeah.

1120
00:53:10,680 --> 00:53:12,780
Man, seriously, this is unbelievable.

1121
00:53:12,780 --> 00:53:18,320
Stop doing weird stuff!

1122
00:53:18,320 --> 00:53:21,220
Why did you open the options screen?!

1123
00:53:21,220 --> 00:53:24,420
It doesn't matter either way.

1124
00:53:24,420 --> 00:53:27,420
Let me see you die!

1125
00:53:27,420 --> 00:53:29,520
I had it on the background screen,

1126
00:53:29,520 --> 00:53:31,820
so I went to the bathroom while the escape menu was still open.

1127
00:53:31,820 --> 00:53:33,120
Damn it!

1128
00:53:33,920 --> 00:53:36,420
It shouldn't matter which screen it's on though.

1129
00:53:36,420 --> 00:53:40,220
Well, it respawned so that's fine.

1130
00:53:40,220 --> 00:53:41,220
True.

1131
00:53:41,220 --> 00:53:44,820
Alright, with this—

1132
00:53:44,820 --> 00:53:46,460
we can do it.

1133
00:53:46,460 --> 00:53:47,420
Where is it?

1134
00:53:47,420 --> 00:53:52,110
Luna's pretty— where'd she go, she's already inside, whoa she's in there.

1135
00:53:52,110 --> 00:53:53,020
Whoa.

1136
00:53:53,020 --> 00:53:57,670
Yesterday I was around here with Azu-chan and the others,

1137
00:53:57,670 --> 00:53:59,170
you went that far?

1138
00:53:59,170 --> 00:54:01,770
From around here, on the right—

1139
00:54:02,570 --> 00:54:05,130
there's a good spot near the entrance.

1140
00:54:05,130 --> 00:54:07,610
Is it there?

1141
00:54:07,610 --> 00:54:11,170
It's there, it's there! I can hear it clearly!

1142
00:54:11,170 --> 00:54:14,850
Oh no, is Polka closer? NW

1143
00:54:14,850 --> 00:54:16,390
N, NW

1144
00:54:16,390 --> 00:54:20,230
Oh, I can hear it— it's there, it's there! Moxie, moxie, moxie!

1145
00:54:20,230 --> 00:54:24,160
Moxie, NW, N

1146
00:54:24,160 --> 00:54:25,330
340

1147
00:54:25,330 --> 00:54:29,740
NW, this way?

1148
00:54:30,680 --> 00:54:32,680
Oh! I can see the tank!

1149
00:54:32,680 --> 00:54:36,390
Can I fire? Fire!

1150
00:54:36,390 --> 00:54:38,190
From here—

1151
00:54:38,190 --> 00:54:42,790
Where, where, where? What do you call it? Where do I hit it?

1152
00:54:42,790 --> 00:54:43,790
N

1153
00:54:43,790 --> 00:54:46,590
Hold on! Polka might be closer!

1154
00:54:46,590 --> 00:54:51,260
You're pretty far out in front. Is that spot okay?

1155
00:54:51,260 --> 00:54:54,260
No! Ah— visual, visual, visual on it!

1156
00:54:54,260 --> 00:54:55,760
Nice, nice! Shoot from here!

1157
00:54:55,760 --> 00:54:56,760
I went ahead and shot!

1158
00:54:56,760 --> 00:54:57,760
Go for it!

1159
00:55:00,240 --> 00:55:04,840
Yeah! Crab, crab, crab! I wasn't crabbing— crab!

1160
00:55:04,840 --> 00:55:08,640
Scary, scary! Crab, crab, crab!

1161
00:55:08,640 --> 00:55:11,340
You're drawing a ton of aggro right now.

1162
00:55:11,340 --> 00:55:14,540
I'm kind of doing a pincer attack right now.

1163
00:55:14,540 --> 00:55:18,040
The aggro's on you, so I can shoot freely.

1164
00:55:18,040 --> 00:55:20,840
Yeah, probably. I've got the aggro.

1165
00:55:20,840 --> 00:55:23,140
Crab, crab, crab, crab, crab!

1166
00:55:23,140 --> 00:55:26,440
I can't even see it— where's the tank?

1167
00:55:26,240 --> 00:55:28,500
There it is!

1168
00:55:32,820 --> 00:55:36,220
Surely it won't walk over here, right?

1169
00:55:36,410 --> 00:55:42,220
After all that firing, even the enemy must have a cooldown, right?

1170
00:55:42,220 --> 00:55:46,220
No it doesn't! It's right in front of me!

1171
00:55:46,220 --> 00:55:47,220
Po? Po?

1172
00:55:47,220 --> 00:55:49,220
It was right in front of me.

1173
00:55:49,220 --> 00:55:50,220
Are you shooting?

1174
00:55:50,220 --> 00:55:51,220
I'm shooting, I'm shooting!

1175
00:55:51,220 --> 00:55:53,220
It's just a little too close—

1176
00:55:53,220 --> 00:55:55,220
Po, where are you?! You're way too far forward!

1177
00:55:55,220 --> 00:55:58,020
Pull back!

1178
00:55:57,810 --> 00:55:59,370
Get further back!

1179
00:55:59,370 --> 00:56:00,050
Nooo!

1180
00:56:00,050 --> 00:56:00,610
Ahahahaha!

1181
00:56:00,610 --> 00:56:02,570
Why are you there?!

1182
00:56:02,570 --> 00:56:05,040
Why did I die there?!

1183
00:56:05,040 --> 00:56:07,920
I'm over here— over here!

1184
00:56:07,920 --> 00:56:14,170
Ah! Polka's bed...

1185
00:56:14,170 --> 00:56:14,850
I died!

1186
00:56:14,850 --> 00:56:17,330
She's dead!

1187
00:56:17,330 --> 00:56:19,530
I died!

1188
00:56:19,530 --> 00:56:23,810
You can't be that close! Come over here!

1189
00:56:23,810 --> 00:56:26,010
I died!

1190
00:56:26,010 --> 00:56:27,490
From here again... where's the bed?

1191
00:56:27,490 --> 00:56:29,890
Oh no, it's far!

1192
00:56:29,890 --> 00:56:30,430
Whe—

1193
00:56:30,430 --> 00:56:32,910
Now the fight against radiation begins.

1194
00:56:32,910 --> 00:56:37,710
The suit— let me head back and drop off the suit.

1195
00:56:37,710 --> 00:56:43,670
Or give me a bed.

1196
00:56:43,670 --> 00:56:47,410
You can give me the camper van bed.

1197
00:56:47,410 --> 00:56:51,070
Hold on, I'm heading back to the camper van.

1198
00:56:51,070 --> 00:56:55,780
Hey, the cannon's flying over there.

1199
00:56:55,780 --> 00:56:59,670
Wait, the camper van was pretty far ahead.

1200
00:57:00,980 --> 00:57:02,980
Ugh...

1201
00:57:02,980 --> 00:57:09,060
The camper van... yeah, that's bad...

1202
00:57:09,060 --> 00:57:10,060


1203
00:57:10,060 --> 00:57:12,740
Ow ow ow ow! I'm getting shot! I'm getting shot!

1204
00:57:12,740 --> 00:57:16,660
Practice and the real thing with Polka watching are totally different.

1205
00:57:16,660 --> 00:57:18,460
It's nerve-wracking.

1206
00:57:18,460 --> 00:57:25,340
Right, next time have them stay about 100... 150 meters back.

1207
00:57:25,340 --> 00:57:28,140
Yeah, it's a bit nerve-wracking.

1208
00:57:28,140 --> 00:57:31,790
Polka's also freaking out right now from the sound of a boar.

1209
00:57:31,790 --> 00:57:34,740
Wait, should I give this sleeping bag to a friend?

1210
00:57:34,740 --> 00:57:36,740
Yeah, yeah, exactly.

1211
00:57:36,740 --> 00:57:38,540
Oh, an airdrop!

1212
00:57:38,540 --> 00:57:40,340
Thanks.

1213
00:57:40,340 --> 00:57:42,340
Should I put one suit back?

1214
00:57:42,340 --> 00:57:45,140
There's a hazmat suit here—

1215
00:57:45,140 --> 00:57:46,940
—wait, there isn't.

1216
00:57:46,940 --> 00:57:48,940
Um...

1217
00:57:48,940 --> 00:57:53,200
Can we do this?

1218
00:57:53,200 --> 00:57:54,200
Hmm...

1219
00:57:54,200 --> 00:57:57,000
Oh, right.

1220
00:57:57,000 --> 00:57:58,880
Should I back off since it's dangerous here?

1221
00:57:58,880 --> 00:58:00,680
What do I do here? Respawn?

1222
00:58:00,680 --> 00:58:01,620
Wait, what was it again?

1223
00:58:01,620 --> 00:58:02,460
Umm...

1224
00:58:02,460 --> 00:58:04,720
Do I just go down here?

1225
00:58:04,720 --> 00:58:07,500
I can't move here.

1226
00:58:07,500 --> 00:58:11,120
Do I just... die here? What am I supposed to do?

1227
00:58:11,120 --> 00:58:13,440
I'm so confused.

1228
00:58:13,440 --> 00:58:15,780
Do I just respawn?

1229
00:58:15,780 --> 00:58:17,280
Okay.

1230
00:58:17,280 --> 00:58:20,980
Let me get a bit further away.

1231
00:58:21,560 --> 00:58:24,640
This car is pretty close to the tank.

1232
00:58:24,640 --> 00:58:27,900
That's what threw me off.

1233
00:58:27,900 --> 00:58:32,810
I misjudged the distance to the tank.

1234
00:58:32,810 --> 00:58:36,830
How about around here?

1235
00:58:36,830 --> 00:58:40,090
Got it.

1236
00:58:40,090 --> 00:58:40,890
Okay...

1237
00:58:40,890 --> 00:58:43,610
How's that?

1238
00:58:43,610 --> 00:58:45,630
Alright, let me just—

1239
00:58:45,630 --> 00:58:47,030
Here I go.

1240
00:58:47,030 --> 00:58:53,340
Where am I right now?

1241
00:58:53,340 --> 00:58:55,540
You'll spawn right there.

1242
00:58:55,540 --> 00:58:58,360
Wow, I ended up way far away.

1243
00:58:58,360 --> 00:58:58,820
Hello!

1244
00:58:58,820 --> 00:59:00,260
I'm far away.

1245
00:59:00,260 --> 00:59:04,140
I went to a small hill.

1246
00:59:04,140 --> 00:59:05,900
Taking damage.

1247
00:59:05,900 --> 00:59:08,760
A small hill.

1248
00:59:08,760 --> 00:59:12,360
There should be a hazmat suit there too.

1249
00:59:12,360 --> 00:59:13,260
Thanks.

1250
00:59:13,260 --> 00:59:14,260
Oh~

1251
00:59:14,260 --> 00:59:16,740
Una.

1252
00:59:16,740 --> 00:59:17,840
It's Una.

1253
00:59:17,840 --> 00:59:21,820
A sleeping bag — but you can't place one here, it's high radiation.

1254
00:59:21,820 --> 00:59:22,700
Oh, food, right.

1255
00:59:22,700 --> 00:59:23,700
For sure.

1256
00:59:23,700 --> 00:59:26,480
Oh, there's pumpkin!

1257
00:59:26,480 --> 00:59:28,060
Give me some pumpkin!

1258
00:59:28,060 --> 00:59:30,600
Hey hey hey!

1259
00:59:30,600 --> 00:59:32,100
Thanks!

1260
00:59:32,100 --> 00:59:35,420
Earlier—

1261
00:59:35,420 --> 00:59:39,720
If you put it a bit behind Bob, it should be fine.

1262
00:59:39,720 --> 00:59:41,980
I don't think I'm hitting it...

1263
00:59:42,020 --> 00:59:43,700
Not at all.

1264
00:59:43,700 --> 00:59:45,700
Yeah, you can't hit it from this far.

1265
00:59:45,700 --> 00:59:50,360
Right?

1266
00:59:50,360 --> 00:59:51,740
Okay.

1267
00:59:51,740 --> 00:59:53,480
Good thing the tank spawned then.

1268
00:59:53,480 --> 00:59:55,400
Yeah, lucky!

1269
00:59:55,400 --> 00:59:57,840
Good thing we made a reservation.

1270
00:59:57,840 --> 01:00:01,460
Yeah, turns out it was the kind of tank you can't get without a reservation.

1271
01:00:01,460 --> 01:00:04,760
It showed up out of nowhere though!

1272
01:00:04,760 --> 01:00:05,840
True.

1273
01:00:05,840 --> 01:00:11,950
I really want some kind of heads-up that it's coming.

1274
01:00:11,950 --> 01:00:12,830
Heave-ho.

1275
01:00:12,830 --> 01:00:13,770
Heave-ho.

1276
01:00:13,770 --> 01:00:23,770
Come on, come on — like with the helicopter, I want something that says "the tank is currently here."

1277
01:00:24,570 --> 01:00:31,050
Yeah, there's nothing like that. Oh, Kani-chan! Kani-chan, Kani-chan — and around here like this—

1278
01:00:31,050 --> 01:00:34,310
—do this.

1279
01:00:34,890 --> 01:00:41,690
Shoot from the front here, then fall back — you can hear it, the direction is toward the inside.

1280
01:00:41,690 --> 01:00:47,110
Cut the lane — cut the lane, right, I learned that from Matsuri-chan.

1281
01:00:47,110 --> 01:00:53,170
I was pushing too far forward — there's a ton of noise around here.

1282
01:00:53,170 --> 01:00:57,110
It's coming! Visual, visual, visual!

1283
01:00:57,110 --> 01:01:02,590
I shot — nope, didn't hit, it passed right by.

1284
01:01:02,590 --> 01:01:04,030
Visual confirmed!

1285
01:01:04,030 --> 01:01:06,030
What do you mean, visual?!

1286
01:01:06,030 --> 01:01:09,030
I mean I can actually see it!

1287
01:01:09,030 --> 01:01:11,410
Polpol?

1288
01:01:11,410 --> 01:01:13,210
I'm running away!

1289
01:01:13,210 --> 01:01:14,210
No way, it's too scary!

1290
01:01:14,210 --> 01:01:15,470
Go down!

1291
01:01:15,470 --> 01:01:17,800
Down?

1292
01:01:17,800 --> 01:01:19,660
Over here, over here!

1293
01:01:19,660 --> 01:01:21,260


1294
01:01:21,260 --> 01:01:23,340
Wait, where are you, Polpol?

1295
01:01:23,340 --> 01:01:24,840
Down here, inside this place.

1296
01:01:24,840 --> 01:01:32,220
Okay, okay, okay!

1297
01:01:32,220 --> 01:01:33,360
I'm in here.

1298
01:01:33,360 --> 01:01:35,360
There you are!

1299
01:01:36,970 --> 01:01:39,510
This is the route Azu-chan showed me yesterday.

1300
01:01:39,510 --> 01:01:41,510
Can the tank even get in here?

1301
01:01:41,510 --> 01:01:43,850
It can't, so we hide here.

1302
01:01:43,850 --> 01:01:47,440
The tank's still out there...

1303
01:01:47,440 --> 01:01:50,230
It is!

1304
01:01:50,230 --> 01:01:52,910
Are the NPCs getting more active?

1305
01:01:52,910 --> 01:01:58,170
They're not running around, but they're there if you peek out.

1306
01:01:58,170 --> 01:01:59,490
You're right.

1307
01:01:59,490 --> 01:02:04,130
I've never been over this way.

1308
01:02:04,130 --> 01:02:07,490
They're waiting for us to come out!

1309
01:02:07,580 --> 01:02:10,090
Wait — are we trapped like rats in a bag here?

1310
01:02:10,090 --> 01:02:14,000
Let's go out from somewhere else.

1311
01:02:14,000 --> 01:02:15,640
Oh, this...

1312
01:02:15,640 --> 01:02:17,400
Oh! Wait! NPCs are coming!

1313
01:02:17,400 --> 01:02:20,600
Wait, are these NPCs? They're not carrying guns — interesting.

1314
01:02:20,600 --> 01:02:22,460
Oh, there they are.

1315
01:02:22,460 --> 01:02:24,880
They're not armed — Kanata, help!

1316
01:02:24,880 --> 01:02:27,780
Apparently once the NPCs break, we should fall back for now.

1317
01:02:27,780 --> 01:02:28,580
Got it.

1318
01:02:28,580 --> 01:02:30,300
But fall back to where?

1319
01:02:30,300 --> 01:02:32,800
Kanata doesn't really know this map either...

1320
01:02:32,800 --> 01:02:34,800
Oh, I think I just went Pol-hate.

1321
01:02:37,370 --> 01:02:40,370
Should we head out from the Ponpon side?

1322
01:02:40,370 --> 01:02:48,320
Heave-ho, heave-ho, heave-ho.

1323
01:02:48,320 --> 01:02:52,720
Looks like it's around NE.

1324
01:02:52,720 --> 01:02:54,640
Oh, I'm back to friendly now.

1325
01:02:54,640 --> 01:02:56,440
Where did the tank go?

1326
01:02:56,440 --> 01:02:58,240
The tank went that way too.

1327
01:02:58,240 --> 01:03:01,040
It's around NE 60 direction.

1328
01:03:01,040 --> 01:03:02,840
NE 60, copy.

1329
01:03:02,840 --> 01:03:03,660
That's far.

1330
01:03:03,660 --> 01:03:06,640
Alright, let's aim from here.

1331
01:03:15,070 --> 01:03:17,070
Not hitting it, huh.

1332
01:03:17,070 --> 01:03:21,310
The tank went back to its original position.

1333
01:03:21,310 --> 01:03:24,760
It went back in front of the room.

1334
01:03:24,760 --> 01:03:26,560
I see.

1335
01:03:26,560 --> 01:03:29,760
Where even is its original position?

1336
01:03:29,760 --> 01:03:33,060
We need to go recover Polka's body.

1337
01:03:33,060 --> 01:03:34,860
Or the respawn will kick in.

1338
01:03:34,860 --> 01:03:37,310
Wait, Polpol's body?

1339
01:03:37,310 --> 01:03:39,310
Oh, it's by that little hill.

1340
01:03:39,310 --> 01:03:41,310
Oh right, I forgot — where was it again?!

1341
01:03:41,310 --> 01:03:43,010
Over that way.

1342
01:03:43,010 --> 01:03:44,410
The little hill.

1343
01:03:44,410 --> 01:03:46,410
The little hill, huh... that's a bit scary.

1344
01:03:46,410 --> 01:03:50,470
Yeah, the tank is...

1345
01:03:50,470 --> 01:03:54,530
It was pretty close, wasn't it.

1346
01:03:54,530 --> 01:03:57,010
Around the M8 marker — thanks.

1347
01:03:57,010 --> 01:03:58,890
Looks like we can go now, right?

1348
01:03:58,890 --> 01:04:00,930
Which way?

1349
01:04:00,930 --> 01:04:02,350
NE 40.

1350
01:04:02,350 --> 01:04:04,300
Around this area.

1351
01:04:04,300 --> 01:04:08,290
Around here, right? Checking the radar.

1352
01:04:08,290 --> 01:04:10,430
Hm?

1353
01:04:10,430 --> 01:04:12,810
Wasn't it around here? There it is — this, this, this!

1354
01:04:12,810 --> 01:04:14,110
It was at the thank-you spot.

1355
01:04:14,110 --> 01:04:15,030
This, this, this!

1356
01:04:15,030 --> 01:04:16,910
Without this scope I'm completely useless.

1357
01:04:16,910 --> 01:04:17,910
Can't see a thing without it.

1358
01:04:17,910 --> 01:04:24,310
You're too far forward — get back, get back!

1359
01:04:24,310 --> 01:04:27,410
I can't even hear the tank anymore.

1360
01:04:27,410 --> 01:04:29,410
Silence... it's quiet.

1361
01:04:29,410 --> 01:04:31,210
From around here,

1362
01:04:31,210 --> 01:04:33,210
grab the loot and fall back.

1363
01:04:33,210 --> 01:04:38,710
The tank is probably...

1364
01:04:38,710 --> 01:04:40,710
Oh, it's inside the tank area.

1365
01:04:40,710 --> 01:04:42,010
It's on patrol, right?

1366
01:04:42,010 --> 01:04:44,010
Yeah, yeah, exactly.

1367
01:04:44,010 --> 01:04:46,320
It's right here.

1368
01:04:46,320 --> 01:04:48,620
Hm? Oh, is that Kanata?

1369
01:04:48,620 --> 01:04:52,190
I was hoping it'd come this way.

1370
01:04:52,190 --> 01:04:54,490
A guided missile? Guided round?

1371
01:04:54,490 --> 01:04:55,790
Yeah.

1372
01:04:55,790 --> 01:05:02,560
It's there!

1373
01:05:02,560 --> 01:05:07,790
Where?

1374
01:05:07,790 --> 01:05:14,680
It's there, but it looks like it might hit a wall.

1375
01:05:14,680 --> 01:05:19,940
Which direction?

1376
01:05:20,240 --> 01:05:23,090
Where is it...

1377
01:05:23,090 --> 01:05:25,890
I can hear it but I can't see it.

1378
01:05:25,890 --> 01:05:26,890
There it is!

1379
01:05:26,890 --> 01:05:28,690
Over by N20.

1380
01:05:28,690 --> 01:05:29,490
N20, copy.

1381
01:05:29,490 --> 01:05:31,490
It's shifted right, toward N30.

1382
01:05:31,490 --> 01:05:37,770
It's in the shadow.

1383
01:05:37,770 --> 01:05:41,570
I lost sight of the tank!

1384
01:05:41,570 --> 01:05:45,570
Yesterday the tank wouldn't come out either.

1385
01:05:45,570 --> 01:05:47,370
You said you got it stuck, right?

1386
01:05:47,370 --> 01:05:50,270
Apparently there was a spot where it got stuck.

1387
01:05:50,270 --> 01:05:54,170
It got stuck in the second half and we just kept shooting it.

1388
01:05:54,170 --> 01:05:56,970
Was black smoke coming out? Were we hitting it?

1389
01:05:56,970 --> 01:05:58,770
Excellent!

1390
01:05:58,770 --> 01:05:59,770
Well done!

1391
01:05:59,770 --> 01:06:03,770
There's smoke! It's there, it's there! Around NE50, 40!

1392
01:06:03,770 --> 01:06:05,570
It's there, it's there!

1393
01:06:05,570 --> 01:06:08,370
Come over here!

1394
01:06:08,370 --> 01:06:11,660
It's coming!

1395
01:06:11,660 --> 01:06:13,560
It's coming, it's coming!

1396
01:06:13,560 --> 01:06:16,360
Does a hit sound different somehow?

1397
01:06:16,360 --> 01:06:18,360
It makes like a "PSSHH!" sound.

1398
01:06:18,360 --> 01:06:20,360
I want to hear that sound.

1399
01:06:20,360 --> 01:06:25,010
I wanna hear that sound!

1400
01:06:33,950 --> 01:06:35,750
Let me hear you cry!

1401
01:06:35,750 --> 01:06:38,550
It's veering off.

1402
01:06:38,550 --> 01:06:43,000
This sound is no good.

1403
01:06:43,000 --> 01:06:46,800
It came this way.

1404
01:06:46,800 --> 01:06:54,010
Not even close.

1405
01:06:54,010 --> 01:06:56,810
What terrible aim.

1406
01:06:57,810 --> 01:07:01,430
Whoa whoa whoa whoa!

1407
01:07:01,430 --> 01:07:03,230
Where? Right now?

1408
01:07:03,230 --> 01:07:08,030
N, N10, N3... I can't tell where 3 is.

1409
01:07:08,030 --> 01:07:09,830
Should we go?

1410
01:07:09,830 --> 01:07:15,500
Kanatan's getting shelled.

1411
01:07:15,500 --> 01:07:19,720
Over there, around N10.

1412
01:07:19,720 --> 01:07:22,520
It went inside, it went inside!

1413
01:07:22,520 --> 01:07:24,520
Oh no, oh no...

1414
01:07:24,520 --> 01:07:29,570
Whoa!

1415
01:07:29,570 --> 01:07:35,330
Getting out this way is gonna be rough.

1416
01:07:35,330 --> 01:07:38,710
Can't peek out here either.

1417
01:07:38,710 --> 01:07:39,670
Where is it?

1418
01:07:39,670 --> 01:07:43,570
Will it back up?

1419
01:07:43,570 --> 01:07:47,410
Okay, fall back.

1420
01:07:47,410 --> 01:07:51,170
Can't see it.

1421
01:07:51,170 --> 01:07:52,870
Enemy soldiers.

1422
01:07:52,870 --> 01:07:59,430
None around.

1423
01:07:59,430 --> 01:08:02,010
Did it go on patrol somewhere again?

1424
01:08:06,250 --> 01:08:10,050
It's gone, wandered off somewhere again.

1425
01:08:10,050 --> 01:08:11,950
Come on, get over here!

1426
01:08:11,950 --> 01:08:15,750
Oh, but it's there — around N40.

1427
01:08:15,750 --> 01:08:19,560
It's there, I can see its eye thing.

1428
01:08:19,560 --> 01:08:21,360
Nice!

1429
01:08:21,360 --> 01:08:25,160
But it's a bit too far to fire a missile.

1430
01:08:25,160 --> 01:08:26,960
The other way?

1431
01:08:26,960 --> 01:08:30,000
I can only see its head.

1432
01:08:30,000 --> 01:08:32,100
It's hiding!

1433
01:08:32,100 --> 01:08:34,440
Can't see it — is it hiding too?

1434
01:08:34,440 --> 01:08:35,860
It's hiding.

1435
01:08:35,860 --> 01:08:37,260
Oh! You're right!

1436
01:08:37,260 --> 01:08:39,140
I can see the turret too!

1437
01:08:39,140 --> 01:08:41,060
Let's just shoot for now.

1438
01:08:41,060 --> 01:08:43,560
An airdrop is casually falling down over there.

1439
01:08:43,560 --> 01:08:49,480
Hey, is it stuck again? That thing?

1440
01:08:49,480 --> 01:08:50,840
Oh, then we can just get it stuck again!

1441
01:08:50,840 --> 01:08:52,440
I have no idea.

1442
01:08:52,440 --> 01:08:55,440
But even if it's stuck, it'll still attack.

1443
01:08:55,440 --> 01:08:56,280
Really?

1444
01:08:56,280 --> 01:08:58,880
We just have to sidestep to dodge.

1445
01:09:03,440 --> 01:09:06,440
You're right, it's trying to start moving.

1446
01:09:06,440 --> 01:09:11,760
Wait, isn't this our chance?

1447
01:09:11,760 --> 01:09:13,360
Hit it!

1448
01:09:13,360 --> 01:09:15,160
In the match!

1449
01:09:15,160 --> 01:09:16,960
Oh, so close!

1450
01:09:16,960 --> 01:09:18,760
A little too high.

1451
01:09:18,760 --> 01:09:20,760
This is tricky.

1452
01:09:20,760 --> 01:09:26,890
It's gonna hit!

1453
01:09:26,890 --> 01:09:29,890
If it's the same as before—

1454
01:09:29,890 --> 01:09:32,690
That thing is seriously stuck.

1455
01:09:32,690 --> 01:09:34,490
Probably because of the slope or something.

1456
01:09:34,490 --> 01:09:36,290
Oh, this is totally not working.

1457
01:09:36,290 --> 01:09:41,760
Yeah, something's off.

1458
01:09:41,760 --> 01:09:45,560
Right, it's really hard to hit from here.

1459
01:09:45,560 --> 01:09:47,360
Too high again.

1460
01:09:47,360 --> 01:09:48,360
Wait, where was it again?

1461
01:09:48,360 --> 01:09:49,360
Too high.

1462
01:09:49,360 --> 01:09:51,160
Like a guided missile or something.

1463
01:09:51,160 --> 01:09:53,160
Someone said aim just a tiny bit higher.

1464
01:09:53,160 --> 01:09:54,160
Just a tiny bit higher, got it.

1465
01:09:54,160 --> 01:09:59,940
Oh, it's heading toward Luna!

1466
01:09:59,940 --> 01:10:07,860
It's breaking line of sight nicely.

1467
01:10:07,860 --> 01:10:14,680


1468
01:10:14,680 --> 01:10:21,410
Oh, did that hit?

1469
01:10:21,410 --> 01:10:23,230
Nice, nice! It's on fire!

1470
01:10:23,230 --> 01:10:24,550
It's burning!

1471
01:10:24,550 --> 01:10:29,710
Keep going, keep going!

1472
01:10:29,710 --> 01:10:37,740
It's fully targeting Luna, so that's a big help.

1473
01:10:37,740 --> 01:10:39,580
Ow!

1474
01:10:39,580 --> 01:10:43,920
Wait, I can't even see it anymore, it's all on fire.

1475
01:10:50,930 --> 01:10:52,930
Alright, let's aim again!

1476
01:10:52,930 --> 01:10:56,910
Getting close is scary though.

1477
01:10:56,910 --> 01:10:59,650
Yeah, getting close is a bad idea.

1478
01:10:59,650 --> 01:11:05,310
It keeps hitting that weird white wall — is it okay?

1479
01:11:05,310 --> 01:11:08,110
Did it hit?

1480
01:11:08,110 --> 01:11:16,910
It keeps bouncing off that white wall, so it's better to aim from this side — but shots are coming, so we have to sidestep to dodge.

1481
01:11:17,710 --> 01:11:19,710
Kanata, where are you?

1482
01:11:19,710 --> 01:11:24,680
Missed by a bit.

1483
01:11:24,680 --> 01:11:29,120
Wait, is that a h-h-h-helicopter?!

1484
01:11:29,120 --> 01:11:30,120
Nope.

1485
01:11:30,120 --> 01:11:31,420
That thing—

1486
01:11:31,420 --> 01:11:32,720
Up ahead—

1487
01:11:32,720 --> 01:11:39,120
That thing is clearly looking right at us!

1488
01:11:39,120 --> 01:11:41,720
W-w-w-wait, wait, wait!

1489
01:11:41,720 --> 01:11:44,520
I haven't done anything wrong, please stop!

1490
01:11:45,320 --> 01:11:47,720
I'm a law-abiding citizen!

1491
01:11:47,720 --> 01:11:49,420
Are we okay? Is this okay?

1492
01:11:49,420 --> 01:11:51,720
We're fine, we're just nearby, that's all.

1493
01:11:51,720 --> 01:11:53,220
Oh no no no no no!

1494
01:11:53,220 --> 01:11:55,220
Oh no no no no no!

1495
01:11:55,220 --> 01:11:56,420
No no no no no no!

1496
01:11:56,420 --> 01:11:58,620
No no no no! I haven't done anything!

1497
01:11:58,620 --> 01:12:00,120
Why?!

1498
01:12:00,120 --> 01:12:04,510
Ow ow ow ow ow!

1499
01:12:04,510 --> 01:12:06,710
That's horrible! Ow ow ow ow ow!

1500
01:12:06,710 --> 01:12:09,310
Why though?!

1501
01:12:09,310 --> 01:12:11,110
That's way too much!

1502
01:12:11,110 --> 01:12:14,110
It's going indiscriminate!

1503
01:12:14,710 --> 01:12:19,070
What are we supposed to do about the tank?!

1504
01:12:19,070 --> 01:12:26,930
If it somehow recovers health after this, I don't know what we'd do—

1505
01:12:26,930 --> 01:12:30,980
I don't think it'll recover — but the helicopter!

1506
01:12:30,980 --> 01:12:35,470
That thing's backup! Just go away!

1507
01:12:35,470 --> 01:12:41,830
How many shots does it take to bring down a helicopter? And this one just showed up!

1508
01:12:41,830 --> 01:12:51,520
No way, no way! We're gonna die! No way! What even is that thing?!

1509
01:12:51,520 --> 01:12:59,980
Why do they roll out the red carpet like this whenever WE do something? Like, it's really something.

1510
01:12:59,980 --> 01:13:09,980
Hey, it's still here, isn't it? Still here, still here. It's just wandering around. Why is it even in this area? It's patrolling too.

1511
01:13:11,060 --> 01:13:15,330
Hey, go home already!

1512
01:13:15,330 --> 01:13:20,700
Polka's inventory is empty — I'm not carrying any guns or anything.

1513
01:13:20,700 --> 01:13:26,020
Don't look at me — how would you even know I have guns in my inventory? That doesn't make sense.

1514
01:13:26,020 --> 01:13:30,580
It's just circling around!

1515
01:13:30,580 --> 01:13:36,000
Well, we've been spotted now, so whatever — you can take it down in 4 shots, Akai-san.

1516
01:13:36,000 --> 01:13:37,580
That's about Akai-san, not us.

1517
01:13:37,580 --> 01:13:38,680
You can do it in 4 shots?

1518
01:13:38,680 --> 01:13:39,480
4 shots and you...

1519
01:13:39,480 --> 01:13:41,480
Oh, its movement just changed completely!

1520
01:13:41,480 --> 01:13:47,700
Hey, could you stop with the anti-air fire?!

1521
01:13:47,700 --> 01:13:49,300
This is seriously bad.

1522
01:13:49,300 --> 01:13:52,200
We're getting attacked from both Ric and Coo!

1523
01:13:52,200 --> 01:13:53,400
Oh, it moved away!

1524
01:13:53,400 --> 01:13:54,400
Luna got chased off!

1525
01:13:54,400 --> 01:13:55,100
Did it leave?

1526
01:13:55,100 --> 01:13:56,900
I want to wait just a little longer, but...

1527
01:13:56,900 --> 01:13:58,800
Goodbye!

1528
01:13:58,800 --> 01:14:00,700
Get out of here!

1529
01:14:00,700 --> 01:14:03,100
W-wait, is it leaving?

1530
01:14:03,100 --> 01:14:04,700
Yeah, it's leaving, it's really leaving right now!

1531
01:14:04,700 --> 01:14:05,500
It's gone, it's gone!

1532
01:14:05,500 --> 01:14:08,540
Oh, it's gonna be nighttime soon.

1533
01:14:08,540 --> 01:14:12,560
And things were going so well...

1534
01:14:12,560 --> 01:14:18,120
Goodbye, goodbye! Please don't come back for a while!

1535
01:14:18,120 --> 01:14:20,990
Phew, what was that all about?

1536
01:14:20,990 --> 01:14:24,160
Things were going so well too...

1537
01:14:24,160 --> 01:14:28,680
When they get cornered, they start firing like crazy.

1538
01:14:28,680 --> 01:14:30,680
Oh, it's still stuck!

1539
01:14:30,680 --> 01:14:36,830
It's still stuck, huh.

1540
01:14:36,830 --> 01:14:38,830
Stay stuck, please, I'm begging you!

1541
01:14:38,830 --> 01:14:44,520
Oh, nice!

1542
01:14:44,520 --> 01:14:47,740
I can hear the hits landing.

1543
01:14:47,740 --> 01:14:49,740
Hime, are we doing a night battle? Oh wait, did you already open the rock?

1544
01:14:49,740 --> 01:14:52,540
No, it should be getting dark soon.

1545
01:14:52,540 --> 01:14:53,540
Huh?

1546
01:14:53,540 --> 01:14:56,860
Oh, did we get it?

1547
01:14:56,860 --> 01:14:57,820
Wait, what?

1548
01:14:57,820 --> 01:15:00,660
We did it, Hime! We're doing it!

1549
01:15:00,660 --> 01:15:01,460
Did we get it?

1550
01:15:01,460 --> 01:15:02,460
The battle is over!

1551
01:15:02,460 --> 01:15:03,460
It's finally over!

1552
01:15:03,460 --> 01:15:05,460
The battle is over!

1553
01:15:05,460 --> 01:15:08,660
The battle is done!

1554
01:15:08,660 --> 01:15:10,460
The battle is over!

1555
01:15:10,460 --> 01:15:13,260
While Polka was struggling,

1556
01:15:13,260 --> 01:15:15,260
Kanata landed all the hits.

1557
01:15:15,260 --> 01:15:18,060
Polka was shooting too!

1558
01:15:18,060 --> 01:15:20,060
Polka was shooting too!

1559
01:15:20,060 --> 01:15:23,860
I was hitting it, I was hitting it!

1560
01:15:23,860 --> 01:15:26,860
Being stuck is so powerful.

1561
01:15:26,860 --> 01:15:28,660
We've lost to the stuck mechanic like three times ourselves though.

1562
01:15:28,660 --> 01:15:29,660
About three times.

1563
01:15:30,480 --> 01:15:36,100
The stuck count here... it's on fire!

1564
01:15:36,100 --> 01:15:44,000
It's super hot! Like, when the fire goes out, three crates appear, and you can't get close to the fire while collecting them—

1565
01:15:44,000 --> 01:15:47,300
you're not supposed to go near it!

1566
01:15:47,290 --> 01:15:49,260
Hot hot hot hot hot hot hot hot!

1567
01:15:49,260 --> 01:15:52,760
Yeah, it burns! Yesterday my belly got burned too~

1568
01:15:52,760 --> 01:15:53,760
It's like...

1569
01:15:55,030 --> 01:15:59,760
It just draws you in. Congrats~!

1570
01:15:59,760 --> 01:16:01,260
We did it~!

1571
01:16:01,260 --> 01:16:05,260
It feels great when it shows up on the map for everyone to see.

1572
01:16:06,580 --> 01:16:08,260
Oh, you're right!

1573
01:16:08,260 --> 01:16:09,760
For everyone to see—

1574
01:16:09,760 --> 01:16:12,260
that we pulled it off!

1575
01:16:12,260 --> 01:16:14,760
We did it~!

1576
01:16:14,870 --> 01:16:17,100
Wooo~!

1577
01:16:16,890 --> 01:16:21,790
Ah, a commemorative photo— I forgot to bring a camera!

1578
01:16:21,790 --> 01:16:26,610
Screenshot, screenshot! We don't have a camera.

1579
01:16:26,610 --> 01:16:30,830
Phew~ Yesterday's practice...

1580
01:16:30,830 --> 01:16:36,020
really paid off. What paid off was yesterday's...

1581
01:16:36,020 --> 01:16:42,270
Without Kanata's practice, Polka definitely would've— teaching her was really tough too.

1582
01:16:42,270 --> 01:16:45,270
Why did you both end up all wrapped in bandages?

1583
01:16:45,270 --> 01:16:49,070
It was seriously rough.

1584
01:16:49,070 --> 01:16:54,670
So this is the end of our battle, huh.

1585
01:16:54,670 --> 01:16:57,470
Yeah, finally.

1586
01:16:57,470 --> 01:17:01,270
Finally, we have no more...

1587
01:17:01,270 --> 01:17:03,950
...regrets?

1588
01:17:03,950 --> 01:17:05,870
No regrets?

1589
01:17:05,870 --> 01:17:06,870
Is there still something left?

1590
01:17:06,870 --> 01:17:10,470
I feel like we worked pretty hard.

1591
01:17:10,270 --> 01:17:12,430
We really did work hard.

1592
01:17:12,430 --> 01:17:14,530
We did it!

1593
01:17:14,530 --> 01:17:17,530
What about the heli? The heli is insane.

1594
01:17:17,530 --> 01:17:19,010
The stupid heli is stupid.

1595
01:17:19,010 --> 01:17:20,550
The heli seems really rough.

1596
01:17:20,550 --> 01:17:21,590
The heli though...

1597
01:17:21,590 --> 01:17:24,830
But if you hit it enough, it goes down, right?

1598
01:17:24,830 --> 01:17:26,510
That's impressive too.

1599
01:17:26,510 --> 01:17:28,610
Even we'd die if a missile hit us.

1600
01:17:28,610 --> 01:17:30,490
That's true.

1601
01:17:30,490 --> 01:17:33,750
There's no way to dodge a heli like that.

1602
01:17:33,750 --> 01:17:36,450
The crab seems impossible too, right?

1603
01:17:36,450 --> 01:17:38,650
Forget the crab — a heli is a whole other level.

1604
01:17:38,470 --> 01:17:41,310
I don't know how to deal with a heli.

1605
01:17:41,310 --> 01:17:46,910
Homing launcher.

1606
01:17:46,910 --> 01:17:48,930
Homing launcher.

1607
01:17:48,930 --> 01:17:50,090
Homing missile.

1608
01:17:50,090 --> 01:17:51,330
I wonder...

1609
01:17:51,330 --> 01:17:53,210
Oh, there's a homing one?

1610
01:17:53,210 --> 01:17:55,310
Oh right, we had a homing one at the base!

1611
01:17:55,310 --> 01:17:56,810
Yeah, we did!

1612
01:17:56,810 --> 01:17:58,710
I see.

1613
01:17:58,710 --> 01:18:01,710
The crab is impossible.

1614
01:18:01,710 --> 01:18:04,290
Yeah, the crab is definitely impossible.

1615
01:18:04,290 --> 01:18:05,650
The mini heli takes 4 shots.

1616
01:18:05,650 --> 01:18:07,670
That one earlier was the big one though.

1617
01:18:08,490 --> 01:18:13,690
But it's flying in the air, so hitting it seems really hard.

1618
01:18:13,690 --> 01:18:17,290
There's a crate though...

1619
01:18:23,750 --> 01:18:30,270
You can see the crate, but if you go to loot it, the armor is super thick.

1620
01:18:30,270 --> 01:18:33,830
There's no fighting it.

1621
01:18:33,830 --> 01:18:35,270
Oh, I know that spot.

1622
01:18:35,270 --> 01:18:38,110
We can't help ourselves — we see a crate in Rust and we just have to open it.

1623
01:18:38,870 --> 01:18:43,490
Same in real life — see a screw and you want to scrap it.

1624
01:18:43,490 --> 01:18:45,090
Only Super Boo.

1625
01:18:45,090 --> 01:18:49,430
Super Boo!

1626
01:18:49,430 --> 01:18:57,480
It's on fire.

1627
01:18:57,480 --> 01:19:00,640
Hope something good comes out of this.

1628
01:19:00,640 --> 01:19:02,880
What do you want from it?

1629
01:19:02,880 --> 01:19:03,780
The fire...

1630
01:19:03,780 --> 01:19:06,500
It's dying down.

1631
01:19:06,500 --> 01:19:08,840
Come on, cool down faster.

1632
01:19:08,840 --> 01:19:14,820
Still burning strong.

1633
01:19:14,820 --> 01:19:16,480
Still going strong.

1634
01:19:16,480 --> 01:19:21,190
Still going, still going.

1635
01:19:21,190 --> 01:19:23,230
Maybe we should just douse it with water to cool it down.

1636
01:19:23,230 --> 01:19:25,250
I don't think water actually cools it down.

1637
01:19:25,250 --> 01:19:27,690
The fire's going out.

1638
01:19:27,690 --> 01:19:28,390
It's going out?

1639
01:19:28,390 --> 01:19:33,400
I wonder what's inside.

1640
01:19:33,400 --> 01:19:35,100
Kanata is really something...

1641
01:19:35,100 --> 01:19:38,880
Hey, I was hoping we'd get some aim-assist thing too.

1642
01:19:38,880 --> 01:19:39,980
Here we go!

1643
01:19:39,980 --> 01:19:42,560
This is still hot though...

1644
01:19:42,560 --> 01:19:44,280
Oh, it's fine, it's fine!

1645
01:19:44,280 --> 01:19:44,900
We're good already?

1646
01:19:44,900 --> 01:19:46,520
Alright, let's check the first one.

1647
01:19:46,520 --> 01:19:47,700
Here goes!

1648
01:19:47,700 --> 01:19:49,840
Here goes!

1649
01:19:49,840 --> 01:19:51,460
There's a Beancan, but...

1650
01:19:51,460 --> 01:19:57,380
Second one.

1651
01:19:57,380 --> 01:19:59,920
The second one is...

1652
01:19:59,920 --> 01:20:02,960
This one lying on its side.

1653
01:20:02,960 --> 01:20:03,920
Okay.

1654
01:20:03,920 --> 01:20:04,720
Okay.

1655
01:20:04,720 --> 01:20:05,720
Oh, what's this?!

1656
01:20:05,720 --> 01:20:09,510
It dropped, Kanata!

1657
01:20:09,310 --> 01:20:11,310
No way!

1658
01:20:11,310 --> 01:20:13,310
First time getting this!

1659
01:20:13,310 --> 01:20:16,310
What the heck! Try shooting it!

1660
01:20:16,310 --> 01:20:19,310
Of all places, we got it here!

1661
01:20:19,310 --> 01:20:21,310
Let's go!

1662
01:20:21,310 --> 01:20:27,250
All that hard work paid off!

1663
01:20:27,050 --> 01:20:29,050
Let's open the other one too!

1664
01:20:29,050 --> 01:20:30,050
Another one!

1665
01:20:30,050 --> 01:20:33,690
Which one is the other?

1666
01:20:33,690 --> 01:20:34,690
Ready, go!

1667
01:20:34,690 --> 01:20:39,230
Rockets keep coming out.

1668
01:20:39,230 --> 01:20:42,090
It's like the game is forcing us to fire rockets.

1669
01:20:42,090 --> 01:20:43,990
An M249 dropped too?!

1670
01:20:43,990 --> 01:20:47,050
No way, getting an M249 here is insane!

1671
01:20:47,050 --> 01:20:49,630
We actually got it, out of nowhere!

1672
01:20:49,630 --> 01:20:51,350
Totally unexpected!

1673
01:20:51,350 --> 01:20:52,130
Wow...

1674
01:20:52,130 --> 01:20:55,430
We've got no choice but to do something with this tonight.

1675
01:20:55,430 --> 01:20:56,250
At this point...

1676
01:20:56,250 --> 01:20:58,550
We have to use these for something, right?

1677
01:20:58,550 --> 01:20:59,890
We have to do something with them.

1678
01:20:59,890 --> 01:21:03,230
Hey, Luna, shoot the M249!

1679
01:21:03,230 --> 01:21:06,130
Should I fire it?

1680
01:21:06,130 --> 01:21:07,650
Go ahead and try shooting something!

1681
01:21:07,650 --> 01:21:08,690
Should we shoot something?

1682
01:21:08,690 --> 01:21:09,930
Don't test it on Polka though!

1683
01:21:10,330 --> 01:21:12,330
I wonder how much damage it does?

1684
01:21:12,330 --> 01:21:14,990
We need a target for this.

1685
01:21:14,990 --> 01:21:18,910
Whoa! The sound is different!

1686
01:21:18,910 --> 01:21:22,530
Oh right, we can use the jackhammer to break it down.

1687
01:21:22,530 --> 01:21:24,970
Kanata, you try it too. Here.

1688
01:21:24,970 --> 01:21:25,710
Wait, oh—

1689
01:21:25,710 --> 01:21:27,850
Okay, this, this, this, this!

1690
01:21:27,850 --> 01:21:30,430
Over there, over there, over there!

1691
01:21:30,430 --> 01:21:31,310
Can we still break it?

1692
01:21:31,310 --> 01:21:32,210
Wait, is it still hot?

1693
01:21:32,210 --> 01:21:33,470
Over there, over there, over there!

1694
01:22:03,270 --> 01:22:03,870
I think so.

1695
01:22:03,660 --> 01:22:04,300
This thing is heavy.

1696
01:22:04,300 --> 01:22:05,820
The ammo, there's so much ammo!

1697
01:22:05,820 --> 01:22:09,080
The heli too— is the heli too far?

1698
01:22:09,080 --> 01:22:09,880
Is the heli too far away?

1699
01:22:09,880 --> 01:22:11,520
Try holding the LMG too. Here.

1700
01:22:11,520 --> 01:22:14,580
This thing holds 100 rounds?! That's insane. Here.

1701
01:22:14,580 --> 01:22:17,180
Hey, can we shoot that heli?

1702
01:22:17,180 --> 01:22:20,580
Suddenly feeling bold with the LMG?

1703
01:22:20,580 --> 01:22:22,180
Well, I mean—

1704
01:22:22,180 --> 01:22:24,720
It's a bit far away, don't you think?

1705
01:22:24,720 --> 01:22:26,300


1706
01:22:26,300 --> 01:22:29,620
I feel like I've gotten so much stronger!

1707
01:22:29,620 --> 01:22:31,200
It's like a machine gun!

1708
01:22:31,660 --> 01:22:36,260
Whoa, whoa, whoa— but it drifts way up!

1709
01:22:36,260 --> 01:22:38,080
Yeah, the recoil is intense.

1710
01:22:38,080 --> 01:22:41,440
I wonder if there's something to reduce the recoil?

1711
01:22:41,440 --> 01:22:45,780
Like, can you customize it somehow?

1712
01:22:45,780 --> 01:22:47,420
This is insane.

1713
01:22:47,420 --> 01:22:50,980
M249.

1714
01:22:50,980 --> 01:22:53,220
The M249 is no joke!

1715
01:22:53,220 --> 01:22:55,940
Whoa, it was shooting at us from all the way over there?!

1716
01:22:55,940 --> 01:22:58,980
That's awful, I can't forgive it!

1717
01:22:58,980 --> 01:23:03,480
Incredible.

1718
01:23:03,480 --> 01:23:05,120
I can't forgive that tank!

1719
01:23:05,120 --> 01:23:07,200
What if you crouch while shooting?

1720
01:23:07,200 --> 01:23:09,360
Is it easier to shoot while crouching?

1721
01:23:09,360 --> 01:23:13,080
Yeah, it might reduce the recoil a bit.

1722
01:23:13,080 --> 01:23:16,660
I can't believe it actually showed up!

1723
01:23:16,660 --> 01:23:20,990
Polka totally knew it would come!

1724
01:23:20,990 --> 01:23:25,290
Polka knew it!

1725
01:23:31,080 --> 01:23:36,590
The tank, we finally—

1726
01:23:36,590 --> 01:23:38,590
Charcoal!

1727
01:23:38,590 --> 01:23:41,370
Oh, there's a sewing machine!

1728
01:23:41,370 --> 01:23:45,610
We did it!

1729
01:23:45,610 --> 01:23:48,030
Everything just dropped out of it!

1730
01:23:48,030 --> 01:23:51,090
Got the metal fragments too!

1731
01:23:53,010 --> 01:23:55,010
WHAT?!

1732
01:23:55,010 --> 01:23:57,510
That's amazing!

1733
01:23:57,510 --> 01:23:59,710
We did it!

1734
01:23:59,710 --> 01:24:01,510
We did it!

1735
01:24:01,510 --> 01:24:04,510
We actually won!

1736
01:24:04,510 --> 01:24:06,160
We won!

1737
01:24:06,160 --> 01:24:10,100


1738
01:24:10,100 --> 01:24:12,100
HoloLuna is victorious!!!

1739
01:24:12,100 --> 01:24:14,100
Victory!!!

1740
01:24:14,100 --> 01:24:15,900
That was incredible!!!

1741
01:24:15,900 --> 01:24:16,700
We did it!

1742
01:24:16,700 --> 01:24:18,700
That's the M249 for you!

1743
01:24:18,700 --> 01:24:19,500
You jerk!

1744
01:24:19,500 --> 01:24:22,800
I can't believe it showed up on the last day!

1745
01:24:22,800 --> 01:24:26,440
We were a bit of a slow starter, huh.

1746
01:24:26,440 --> 01:24:27,940
For real.

1747
01:24:27,940 --> 01:24:31,100
We were a bit slow to get going, but—

1748
01:24:31,100 --> 01:24:33,880
At least we got to see this thing shine!

1749
01:24:33,880 --> 01:24:39,260
We managed to pull it off in the evening session.

1750
01:24:39,260 --> 01:24:40,340
Somehow.

1751
01:24:40,340 --> 01:24:43,420
Is anything else happening in the evening session?

1752
01:24:43,420 --> 01:24:45,220
Nah, nothing really.

1753
01:24:45,220 --> 01:24:49,480
But hey, we took down the tank!

1754
01:24:49,480 --> 01:24:52,480
That's amazing, we really made the most of it!

1755
01:24:52,480 --> 01:24:55,520
We did!

1756
01:24:55,520 --> 01:24:59,320
We managed to do a lot of things we couldn't do last time!

1757
01:24:59,320 --> 01:25:01,120
Polka got to do so much this time!

1758
01:25:01,120 --> 01:25:03,920
It was my first time fighting the tank!

1759
01:25:03,920 --> 01:25:05,720
Right?!

1760
01:25:05,720 --> 01:25:09,520
Doing this repeatedly would be terrifying — it'd take years off your life.

1761
01:25:09,520 --> 01:25:10,520
Seriously.

1762
01:25:10,520 --> 01:25:12,520
Your lifespan just keeps draining away.

1763
01:25:12,520 --> 01:25:14,120
Doing stuff like this...

1764
01:25:14,120 --> 01:25:16,120
It seems easy but it's actually brutal.

1765
01:25:18,570 --> 01:25:22,570
Well, it was basically stuck the whole time,

1766
01:25:22,570 --> 01:25:25,370
so it felt a little easier, you know?

1767
01:25:25,370 --> 01:25:28,370
That's part of it — it wasn't moving.

1768
01:25:28,370 --> 01:25:30,170
Hello there, Mr. Helicopter!

1769
01:25:30,170 --> 01:25:31,970
Is the heli coming again?

1770
01:25:31,970 --> 01:25:33,790
A little heli—

1771
01:25:33,790 --> 01:25:34,770
A little heli.

1772
01:25:34,770 --> 01:25:37,480
Is it here?

1773
01:25:37,480 --> 01:25:39,280
Nope, nope.

1774
01:25:39,280 --> 01:25:42,280
Since it's just us here, the heli comes all the time.

1775
01:25:42,280 --> 01:25:45,080
Heading straight for us.

1776
01:25:45,080 --> 01:25:46,880
Have we done anything wrong?

1777
01:25:46,880 --> 01:25:48,680
We have.

1778
01:25:48,680 --> 01:25:52,480
We have. The tank.

1779
01:25:52,480 --> 01:25:54,280
We took out the tank.

1780
01:25:54,280 --> 01:25:58,280
But Kanatan still can't log in today, right?

1781
01:25:58,280 --> 01:26:00,190
I do want to report back to her though.

1782
01:26:00,190 --> 01:26:02,080
Yeah, for sure.

1783
01:26:02,080 --> 01:26:04,080
It was her dream, after all.

1784
01:26:04,080 --> 01:26:07,880
To think that we'd get an M249...

1785
01:26:07,880 --> 01:26:11,880
She wanted an M249 from the Golden Egg.

1786
01:26:13,680 --> 01:26:16,500
And we got one from the Face Punch monument.

1787
01:26:16,500 --> 01:26:19,120
Close enough!

1788
01:26:19,120 --> 01:26:20,080
Phew~

1789
01:26:20,080 --> 01:26:21,320
Haah~

1790
01:26:21,320 --> 01:26:25,150
Which one is that?

1791
01:26:25,150 --> 01:26:26,550
Shall we head back?

1792
01:26:26,550 --> 01:26:27,310
Shall we head back?

1793
01:26:27,310 --> 01:26:27,810
Hmm?

1794
01:26:27,810 --> 01:26:29,030
They said we look alike.

1795
01:26:29,030 --> 01:26:30,990
Got complimented on looking alike.

1796
01:26:30,990 --> 01:26:32,150
We look alike.

1797
01:26:32,150 --> 01:26:35,470
Haven't used the recycler yet.

1798
01:26:35,470 --> 01:26:36,570
Hey~

1799
01:26:36,570 --> 01:26:39,970
They're back again~

1800
01:26:42,950 --> 01:26:44,290
Egg Hunt!

1801
01:26:44,290 --> 01:26:47,670
It's Egg Hunt time~ Fun fun Egg Hunt!

1802
01:26:47,670 --> 01:26:50,270
This is NOT the time for that!

1803
01:26:50,270 --> 01:26:53,090
Seriously!

1804
01:26:53,090 --> 01:26:54,770
Right now it's all fun and games—

1805
01:26:54,770 --> 01:26:58,890
We just finished fighting the tank and we're finally breathing again.

1806
01:26:58,890 --> 01:27:02,430
I'm so glad we pulled it off!

1807
01:27:02,430 --> 01:27:04,010
Right, seriously!

1808
01:27:04,010 --> 01:27:05,210
Yesterday was rough.

1809
01:27:05,210 --> 01:27:07,120
Yesterday was hahaha—

1810
01:27:07,120 --> 01:27:09,770
The zombie attack was insane, wasn't it?

1811
01:27:09,770 --> 01:27:12,030
It really was a full-on zombie attack.

1812
01:27:12,030 --> 01:27:17,250
You okay? Think you can make it to Shadow?

1813
01:27:17,250 --> 01:27:19,210
Heading to Shadow now.

1814
01:27:19,210 --> 01:27:20,310
Nice, nice!

1815
01:27:20,310 --> 01:27:23,780
Yay~!

1816
01:27:23,780 --> 01:27:24,800
Yay~!

1817
01:27:24,800 --> 01:27:28,600
Passing the baton of life.

1818
01:27:28,600 --> 01:27:30,200
The baton of life.

1819
01:27:30,200 --> 01:27:31,400
Exactly.

1820
01:27:31,400 --> 01:27:33,440
Polpol—

1821
01:27:33,440 --> 01:27:34,140
Yeah yeah.

1822
01:27:34,140 --> 01:27:34,840
*thud*

1823
01:27:34,840 --> 01:27:37,240
That was a nice one.

1824
01:27:40,660 --> 01:27:43,920
I mean, we both kind of won through bugs,

1825
01:27:43,920 --> 01:27:47,520
and they won because we got stuck — it goes both ways.

1826
01:27:47,520 --> 01:27:48,460
True enough.

1827
01:27:48,460 --> 01:27:48,960
Right?

1828
01:27:48,960 --> 01:27:50,300
50/50.

1829
01:27:50,300 --> 01:27:53,000
We're even.

1830
01:27:53,000 --> 01:27:54,000
Exactly.

1831
01:27:54,000 --> 01:27:55,740
It cancels out.

1832
01:27:55,740 --> 01:27:56,680
Left.

1833
01:27:56,680 --> 01:27:58,560
Okay.

1834
01:27:58,560 --> 01:28:04,480
We took down the tank — are you satisfied now?

1835
01:28:04,480 --> 01:28:07,520
Are we fighting?

1836
01:28:10,700 --> 01:28:12,800
We've done everything we set out to do!

1837
01:28:12,800 --> 01:28:13,700
Dusty...

1838
01:28:13,700 --> 01:28:19,110
There's a heli.

1839
01:28:19,110 --> 01:28:20,310
Heli's here.

1840
01:28:20,310 --> 01:28:21,410
Trainyard.

1841
01:28:21,410 --> 01:28:23,510
Straight ahead, straight ahead.

1842
01:28:23,510 --> 01:28:24,110
Straight ahead, straight ahead.

1843
01:28:24,110 --> 01:28:24,810
Oh, it's not the heli—

1844
01:28:24,810 --> 01:28:25,710
Tank! Tank!

1845
01:28:25,710 --> 01:28:28,210
Go right, go right!

1846
01:28:28,210 --> 01:28:31,410
I can see the base already.

1847
01:28:31,410 --> 01:28:32,110
It's super close.

1848
01:28:32,110 --> 01:28:32,610
Super close.

1849
01:28:32,610 --> 01:28:34,110
Right!

1850
01:28:34,110 --> 01:28:35,710
What happened to the heli?

1851
01:28:35,710 --> 01:28:36,810
What happened to the heli?

1852
01:28:39,870 --> 01:28:42,030
Granny, stop it!

1853
01:28:41,625 --> 01:28:42,625
Wait, wait, wait!

1854
01:28:42,625 --> 01:28:44,625
Left, left — veer left!

1855
01:28:44,625 --> 01:28:46,625
Hold on — heli, heli, it's coming!

1856
01:28:46,625 --> 01:28:48,625
The heli went toward you!

1857
01:28:48,625 --> 01:28:50,625
Oh, it turned back this way!

1858
01:28:50,625 --> 01:28:51,625
Veer left!

1859
01:28:51,625 --> 01:28:52,625
Hold on — heli, heli, it's coming!

1860
01:28:52,625 --> 01:28:53,845
What the—!

1861
01:28:53,450 --> 01:28:56,810


1862
01:29:06,610 --> 01:29:08,610
Help me!

1863
01:29:08,610 --> 01:29:10,610
Help me!

1864
01:29:10,610 --> 01:29:13,970
Hey!

1865
01:29:13,970 --> 01:29:14,970
There's way too many!

1866
01:29:14,970 --> 01:29:17,970
If my M249 burns up, you're gonna pay for it!

1867
01:29:17,810 --> 01:29:18,630
Oh, seriously!

1868
01:29:17,970 --> 01:29:19,970
For real!

1869
01:29:19,970 --> 01:29:28,410
Dying to an explosion is the worst!

1870
01:29:28,410 --> 01:29:32,770
I don't wanna die to an explosion!

1871
01:29:32,770 --> 01:29:34,770
I'm going home!

1872
01:29:35,410 --> 01:29:37,350
That thing is the absolute worst!

1873
01:29:37,350 --> 01:29:40,750
I can't forgive it!

1874
01:29:40,750 --> 01:29:42,390
Ugh!

1875
01:29:42,390 --> 01:29:45,550
I thought I was starting to like the heli a little bit, but...

1876
01:29:45,340 --> 01:29:48,440
Hey, the car is...

1877
01:29:48,440 --> 01:29:50,940
Hey, get in the back! Luna!

1878
01:29:50,940 --> 01:29:52,340
Heli — is the heli okay?

1879
01:29:52,340 --> 01:29:52,940
No idea.

1880
01:29:52,940 --> 01:29:53,740
Is it gone?

1881
01:29:53,740 --> 01:29:55,140
Get in the back.

1882
01:29:55,140 --> 01:29:55,640
You in?

1883
01:29:55,640 --> 01:29:56,540
Yeah, I'm in!

1884
01:29:56,540 --> 01:29:58,740
We'll show it we're harmless.

1885
01:29:58,740 --> 01:30:03,240
Damn it!

1886
01:30:03,240 --> 01:30:10,070
Hey, the camper van broke again.

1887
01:30:10,260 --> 01:30:12,470
Did everything break?

1888
01:30:12,470 --> 01:30:14,940
It breaks every single time.

1889
01:30:14,940 --> 01:30:17,770
Whoa! It's a sea of fire!

1890
01:30:17,770 --> 01:30:18,570
Oh!

1891
01:30:18,570 --> 01:30:19,570
Which one is it?

1892
01:30:19,570 --> 01:30:21,170
Something's coming.

1893
01:30:21,170 --> 01:30:22,970
Someone's here.

1894
01:30:22,970 --> 01:30:24,570
Huh?

1895
01:30:24,570 --> 01:30:26,570
There was a person just now, right?

1896
01:30:26,570 --> 01:30:28,370
Hello!

1897
01:30:28,370 --> 01:30:30,370
Are you okay?

1898
01:30:30,370 --> 01:30:32,170
Our corpses!

1899
01:30:32,170 --> 01:30:34,170
Oh no! Thank you!

1900
01:30:34,170 --> 01:30:35,970
Did the bear take care of it?

1901
01:30:35,970 --> 01:30:37,770
Hot hot hot hot hot!

1902
01:30:37,770 --> 01:30:39,770
Wait, the bear just died on its own!

1903
01:30:39,770 --> 01:30:41,770
The bear died by itself — okay!

1904
01:30:41,770 --> 01:30:46,570
It probably came to eat this person and got burned by the flames.

1905
01:30:46,570 --> 01:30:53,170
Thank you! We're fine! But the camper van broke...

1906
01:30:53,170 --> 01:30:54,830
Oh no, don't worry about it...

1907
01:30:54,830 --> 01:30:57,770
Ah, that happened, huh. I see.

1908
01:30:57,770 --> 01:31:03,570
I was lying down before logging in and there was this huge noise—

1909
01:31:05,120 --> 01:31:07,120
Oh wait, this is Polka's stuff.

1910
01:31:07,120 --> 01:31:09,980
Sorry for scaring you — it's okay!

1911
01:31:09,980 --> 01:31:13,920
No no, it's totally fine, all good, really!

1912
01:31:13,920 --> 01:31:16,720
Where's Unata's body? Oh, is this it?

1913
01:31:16,720 --> 01:31:20,350
There are three bodies lying around, so it should be fine, right?

1914
01:31:20,350 --> 01:31:23,320
The bodies look okay for now.

1915
01:31:23,320 --> 01:31:28,060
Ugh, come on...

1916
01:31:28,060 --> 01:31:29,920
Ahh, that scared me!

1917
01:31:29,920 --> 01:31:31,860
What?

1918
01:31:31,860 --> 01:31:33,660
What is that thing even?

1919
01:31:33,660 --> 01:31:36,260
Hime!

1920
01:31:36,260 --> 01:31:39,510
We died way too many times.

1921
01:31:49,420 --> 01:31:51,420
It wasn't even the tank that got us—

1922
01:31:51,420 --> 01:31:55,300
Was it a mama bear and a cub?

1923
01:31:55,300 --> 01:31:58,100
No way, seriously, old man...

1924
01:31:58,100 --> 01:32:04,070
This time we took damage from something other than the tank.

1925
01:32:04,070 --> 01:32:06,070
We're okay!

1926
01:32:06,070 --> 01:32:09,480
Ahahahaha!

1927
01:32:09,480 --> 01:32:13,480
A bonus bear showed up but we're fine now!

1928
01:32:13,480 --> 01:32:15,480
Hold on!

1929
01:32:15,480 --> 01:32:18,280
Sorry for all the gunfire in the neighborhood!

1930
01:32:18,280 --> 01:32:20,280
Seriously!

1931
01:32:20,280 --> 01:32:24,080
Thanks! Oh, the patrol's back, the patrol's back!

1932
01:32:24,080 --> 01:32:28,080
Ow! Give me back my M249!

1933
01:32:28,080 --> 01:32:31,920
Wait up!

1934
01:32:31,920 --> 01:32:34,720
Ah! I'm being targeted, what do I do?!

1935
01:32:34,720 --> 01:32:35,220
Run...

1936
01:32:35,220 --> 01:32:37,720
We've left way too many corpses in front of Tonchi's place.

1937
01:32:37,720 --> 01:32:38,720
Right?

1938
01:32:38,720 --> 01:32:42,520
What if we hit Niko-tan's house?

1939
01:32:42,520 --> 01:32:45,820
That would be such an accident.

1940
01:32:45,820 --> 01:32:48,620
The bear— wait, are you kidding me?

1941
01:32:48,620 --> 01:32:52,820
I didn't expect two bears to show up.

1942
01:32:52,820 --> 01:32:54,620
Is this— is this Niko-tan's body?

1943
01:32:54,620 --> 01:32:55,420
This one?

1944
01:32:55,420 --> 01:32:56,620
Wait, which one is Niko-tan?

1945
01:32:56,620 --> 01:32:58,420
That one, the blue one.

1946
01:32:58,420 --> 01:33:00,420
Oh, this one, this one!

1947
01:33:00,420 --> 01:33:02,420
Are you kidding me?

1948
01:33:03,740 --> 01:33:05,740
That guy seriously...

1949
01:33:05,740 --> 01:33:07,540
That guy's a total stalker, isn't he?

1950
01:33:07,540 --> 01:33:09,540
I knew it.

1951
01:33:09,540 --> 01:33:13,140
He's way too obsessed with us.

1952
01:33:13,140 --> 01:33:14,940
This is Polka's, right?

1953
01:33:14,940 --> 01:33:16,770
Yeah, which one?

1954
01:33:16,770 --> 01:33:18,740
Under Polka's.

1955
01:33:18,740 --> 01:33:20,740
Oh wait, there's nothing in it.

1956
01:33:20,740 --> 01:33:22,540
This one says "Himemori is here."

1957
01:33:22,540 --> 01:33:24,540
This one's Polka's.

1958
01:33:24,540 --> 01:33:26,420
We've been rolling around in corpses way too much.

1959
01:33:26,420 --> 01:33:28,140
This is the worst.

1960
01:33:28,140 --> 01:33:30,140
The camper van got wrecked too.

1961
01:33:30,140 --> 01:33:31,740
Well, it's not totally destroyed.

1962
01:33:31,740 --> 01:33:34,040
It seems like it can be repaired, more so than last time.

1963
01:33:34,040 --> 01:33:35,320
Oh, you're right.

1964
01:33:35,320 --> 01:33:39,560
Oh, scary.

1965
01:33:39,560 --> 01:33:41,340
But still, you know?

1966
01:33:41,340 --> 01:33:45,600
Can we fix it?

1967
01:33:45,600 --> 01:33:47,360
*banging sounds*

1968
01:33:47,360 --> 01:33:49,060
Hmm...

1969
01:33:49,060 --> 01:33:54,100
That's scary, there's that sound again.

1970
01:33:54,100 --> 01:33:55,800
The sounds are scary.

1971
01:33:55,800 --> 01:33:57,480
Is Eri coming?

1972
01:33:57,940 --> 01:33:59,580
- I don't know. - It's close to me.

1973
01:33:59,580 --> 01:34:02,120
It's just nearby, just nearby, just nearby.

1974
01:34:02,120 --> 01:34:05,130
- Just nearby, just nearby, just nearby. - Mine's scary too.

1975
01:34:05,130 --> 01:34:08,980
I can't tell anymore... I just can't.

1976
01:34:08,980 --> 01:34:11,820
We've been attacked so many times I can't keep track.

1977
01:34:11,820 --> 01:34:14,460
What do those things even want?

1978
01:34:14,460 --> 01:34:17,400
To kill us.

1979
01:34:17,400 --> 01:34:19,020
That's scary!

1980
01:34:19,020 --> 01:34:22,100
I don't have the materials to fix it.

1981
01:34:22,100 --> 01:34:24,760
- Yeah, somehow today— - The materials are all gone.

1982
01:34:24,760 --> 01:34:26,360
We got too visible.

1983
01:34:26,360 --> 01:34:34,980
It's close enough to walk back, so it's fine.

1984
01:34:34,980 --> 01:34:36,260
True.

1985
01:34:36,260 --> 01:34:39,160
We don't even need the car anymore, do we?

1986
01:34:39,160 --> 01:34:42,820
We worked so hard to build it though.

1987
01:34:42,820 --> 01:34:47,420
We lost two cars in just a few hours today.

1988
01:34:47,420 --> 01:34:53,180
The fire spread too fast.

1989
01:34:54,040 --> 01:34:56,040
They got wrecked so quickly~

1990
01:34:56,040 --> 01:34:59,360
Gone so fast~

1991
01:34:59,360 --> 01:35:01,360
They broke way too quickly.

1992
01:35:01,360 --> 01:35:03,360
Alright, we'll just abandon this one. Thanks for your service.

1993
01:35:03,360 --> 01:35:06,820
Thanks~

1994
01:35:06,820 --> 01:35:11,980
It's already half-buried anyway.

1995
01:35:11,980 --> 01:35:17,420
Let's just head home.

1996
01:35:17,420 --> 01:35:22,260
There's trash scattered everywhere.

1997
01:35:23,080 --> 01:35:29,580
"In front of my kouhai's house, you're shooting guns and leaving trash everywhere—"

1998
01:35:29,580 --> 01:35:34,620
"Come on, we were so close to being done!"

1999
01:35:34,620 --> 01:35:40,380
"Seriously! It was right on our doorstep! Our place was literally getting bombed!"

2000
01:35:40,380 --> 01:35:44,240
"I'm so glad— Niko-tan, I'm so glad you're safe."

2001
01:35:44,240 --> 01:35:46,990
"I need to bring Niko-tan some kind of apology gift."

2002
01:35:46,990 --> 01:35:48,980
"We almost got caught in the crossfire."

2003
01:35:48,980 --> 01:35:53,980
For real, Niko-tan's place was getting absolutely bombed, it was crazy.

2004
01:35:53,980 --> 01:35:55,780
It really was.

2005
01:35:55,780 --> 01:35:58,780
I'm glad she's okay. I need to bring her some kind of apology gift.

2006
01:35:58,780 --> 01:36:00,780
What would be good, I wonder?

2007
01:36:00,780 --> 01:36:03,580
Good work out there.

2008
01:36:03,580 --> 01:36:08,180
Kanata-so, bring out the M249!

2009
01:36:08,180 --> 01:36:10,980
I've got an M249 right here!

2010
01:36:10,980 --> 01:36:12,640
Kanata-so, with pleasure!

2011
01:36:12,640 --> 01:36:15,580
Yes! We got the M249!

2012
01:36:16,400 --> 01:36:18,200
Don't point that at me!

2013
01:36:18,200 --> 01:36:22,580
The one with the stars aligned—

2014
01:36:22,580 --> 01:36:24,800
We went and got it ourselves.

2015
01:36:24,800 --> 01:36:27,940
While losing our lives multiple times.

2016
01:36:27,940 --> 01:36:31,640
We died so many times today too.

2017
01:36:31,640 --> 01:36:32,700
It's ridiculous, right?

2018
01:36:32,700 --> 01:36:35,900
You said it was going to go smoothly.

2019
01:36:35,900 --> 01:36:36,560
That was just you.

2020
01:36:36,560 --> 01:36:38,720
We died for nothing.

2021
01:36:38,720 --> 01:36:40,940
Seriously, and not even from the tank!

2022
01:36:40,940 --> 01:36:42,000
Dying this much to random stuff...

2023
01:36:42,000 --> 01:36:46,300
We died more to non-tank stuff than the actual tank.

2024
01:36:46,300 --> 01:36:51,080
What is even going on?

2025
01:36:51,080 --> 01:36:54,180
We did it!

2026
01:36:54,180 --> 01:36:55,960
Well, "we did it" isn't quite right...

2027
01:36:55,960 --> 01:36:56,740
We did do it though.

2028
01:36:56,740 --> 01:36:59,060
Those guys are the ones who actually did it.

2029
01:36:59,060 --> 01:37:00,320
The worst.

2030
01:37:00,320 --> 01:37:03,020
Weirdos.

2031
01:37:03,020 --> 01:37:08,160
Not funny.

2032
01:37:08,160 --> 01:37:17,890
That was rough, but it was so funny — stuff like that really happens in life, huh.

2033
01:37:17,890 --> 01:37:27,890
I'm glad to be alive... well, we managed even after dying, so... I'm glad to be alive but we did die — it's hard to put into words.

2034
01:37:31,040 --> 01:37:37,610
Being alive gives you all kinds of experiences, but we still died, didn't we.

2035
01:37:37,610 --> 01:37:40,210
Alright.

2036
01:37:40,210 --> 01:37:42,210
This and this.

2037
01:37:42,210 --> 01:37:46,290
We grew a little bit today.

2038
01:37:46,290 --> 01:37:47,450
It went down.

2039
01:37:47,450 --> 01:37:52,290
The rocket launcher ammo went up like crazy though.

2040
01:37:52,290 --> 01:37:53,970
Did we end up with more than when we came?

2041
01:37:53,970 --> 01:37:55,590
Maybe not quite that much.

2042
01:37:55,590 --> 01:37:56,590
Did we pick some up?

2043
01:37:56,590 --> 01:37:57,530
Yeah, we picked some up.

2044
01:37:57,530 --> 01:38:00,030
We picked up 6.

2045
01:38:00,030 --> 01:38:01,270
Oh, so we have quite a bit then.

2046
01:38:01,270 --> 01:38:04,230
And homing missiles too.

2047
01:38:04,230 --> 01:38:06,110
So tonight we could maybe do something with these...

2048
01:38:06,110 --> 01:38:07,210
This thing...

2049
01:38:07,210 --> 01:38:07,870
What was it called again?

2050
01:38:07,870 --> 01:38:10,150
Some kind of rocket — is this for the tank?

2051
01:38:10,150 --> 01:38:10,890
Well, not the tank exactly...

2052
01:38:10,890 --> 01:38:12,890
Is it the one you use at the military base?

2053
01:38:12,890 --> 01:38:15,830
Oh, the one that fires missiles?

2054
01:38:15,830 --> 01:38:18,310
This is basically PVP stuff at this point.

2055
01:38:18,310 --> 01:38:19,230
We don't need this.

2056
01:38:19,230 --> 01:38:20,930
Can't use it.

2057
01:38:20,930 --> 01:38:22,670
That thing...

2058
01:38:22,670 --> 01:38:23,890
And we haven't even used it.

2059
01:38:23,890 --> 01:38:24,890
Yeah, we can't really use it.

2060
01:38:24,890 --> 01:38:28,330
Right, there's nowhere to use it.

2061
01:38:28,330 --> 01:38:30,910
Didn't that thing have a pretty long cooldown too?

2062
01:38:30,910 --> 01:38:34,690
I'd like to try taking the military facility once.

2063
01:38:36,490 --> 01:38:37,710
Oh really?

2064
01:38:37,710 --> 01:38:40,110
There were people at the military facility too, right?

2065
01:38:40,110 --> 01:38:44,470
And you hack the missile computer there or something...

2066
01:38:44,470 --> 01:38:47,350
Ugh, I have no idea how missiles work.

2067
01:38:47,350 --> 01:38:49,330
Yeah, I can't fire this thing.

2068
01:38:49,330 --> 01:38:52,690
Maybe it'd be useful in PVP situations...

2069
01:38:52,690 --> 01:38:55,390
But I'd never use 12 of them.

2070
01:38:55,390 --> 01:38:58,150
Is this it — MLRS rockets?

2071
01:38:58,150 --> 01:39:00,030
I'd never use these.

2072
01:39:00,030 --> 01:39:01,810
Yeah, I wouldn't use these.

2073
01:39:01,810 --> 01:39:03,810
Oh, it's the ones you fire from the military base.

2074
01:39:03,810 --> 01:39:04,810
Yeah, exactly, exactly.

2075
01:39:04,810 --> 01:39:07,610
We don't need these!

2076
01:39:07,610 --> 01:39:09,610
Are we really supposed to use these?

2077
01:39:09,610 --> 01:39:11,610
This is too much!

2078
01:39:11,610 --> 01:39:16,850
If this were PVP, we'd be in the strongest position right now.

2079
01:39:16,850 --> 01:39:21,020
Holding all these guns...

2080
01:39:21,020 --> 01:39:23,820
True, but I have no idea how any of it works.

2081
01:39:23,820 --> 01:39:25,820
Yeah, my skills just aren't quite there yet.

2082
01:39:25,820 --> 01:39:31,780
The heli's heading this way again.

2083
01:39:31,780 --> 01:39:33,580
Ugh, this heli...

2084
01:39:33,580 --> 01:39:34,580
This heli, I swear...

2085
01:39:34,580 --> 01:39:37,310
It's already figured out where we are.

2086
01:39:37,310 --> 01:39:38,180
Obviously.

2087
01:39:38,180 --> 01:39:39,980
Should we try shooting at it?

2088
01:39:39,980 --> 01:39:43,580
Huh?

2089
01:39:43,580 --> 01:39:44,380
Hime?

2090
01:39:44,380 --> 01:39:47,250
Homing! Homing! Homing! Homing!

2091
01:39:47,250 --> 01:39:49,180
How many times have those guys taken us out now?

2092
01:39:49,180 --> 01:39:50,180
Homing missiles! Homing!

2093
01:39:50,180 --> 01:39:52,180
Where were the homing missiles again?

2094
01:39:52,180 --> 01:39:57,780
The homing missiles should be over there.

2095
01:39:57,780 --> 01:40:00,680
Isn't it getting closer though?

2096
01:40:00,680 --> 01:40:04,040
We're being targeted!

2097
01:40:04,040 --> 01:40:06,740
The homing— where, where is it?

2098
01:40:06,740 --> 01:40:08,440
Homing missile!

2099
01:40:08,440 --> 01:40:11,280
What is this? Ammo?

2100
01:40:11,280 --> 01:40:12,840
What do I load it into?

2101
01:40:12,840 --> 01:40:15,460
Is this a rocket launcher too?

2102
01:40:15,460 --> 01:40:17,420
It's a homing launcher.

2103
01:40:17,420 --> 01:40:19,740
What do I attach it to, huh?

2104
01:40:19,740 --> 01:40:22,800
What do I put it in... hmm?

2105
01:40:22,800 --> 01:40:25,400
A dedicated launcher? Oh, I think I've seen one.

2106
01:40:25,780 --> 01:40:27,780
Like a homing launcher type thing?

2107
01:40:27,780 --> 01:40:29,580
Do we have one?

2108
01:40:29,580 --> 01:40:31,380
We do.

2109
01:40:31,380 --> 01:40:34,180
This house has everything.

2110
01:40:34,180 --> 01:40:34,980
It's insane.

2111
01:40:34,980 --> 01:40:36,980
This, this, this, this!

2112
01:40:36,980 --> 01:40:38,980
If we fire near the house it'll get destroyed though.

2113
01:40:38,980 --> 01:40:41,780
Move a bit further away and load it up.

2114
01:40:41,780 --> 01:40:42,780
By the way, there's only one.

2115
01:40:42,780 --> 01:40:43,780
Wow, they have this too?

2116
01:40:43,780 --> 01:40:46,580
Wait, let me see if I can craft another one.

2117
01:40:46,580 --> 01:40:47,580
Hurry up!

2118
01:40:47,580 --> 01:40:48,580
The heli—

2119
01:40:48,580 --> 01:40:50,380
The heli's gonna leave!

2120
01:40:50,380 --> 01:40:51,180
The heli leaving is actually a good thing.

2121
01:40:51,180 --> 01:40:53,180
Those guys are only targeting us anyway.

2122
01:40:54,180 --> 01:41:00,120
Rather than causing trouble, let's just go for it — move back a bit.

2123
01:41:00,120 --> 01:41:03,920
Actually, homing—

2124
01:41:03,920 --> 01:41:12,940
Can the homing launcher be crafted as a weapon? If I research it I can make anything, so that's fine.

2125
01:41:12,940 --> 01:41:17,500
I can research it! Oh, I can research it!

2126
01:41:20,370 --> 01:41:25,250
Let's make it. We're gonna show that heli what's what!

2127
01:41:25,250 --> 01:41:30,190
Exactly! We'll track it down with homing missiles!

2128
01:41:30,190 --> 01:41:33,710
Let's bring two homing missiles.

2129
01:41:33,710 --> 01:41:38,250
Sure, let's do it!

2130
01:41:38,250 --> 01:41:43,410
Let's avenge all our past defeats!

2131
01:41:43,570 --> 01:41:52,590
Wait, the materials — it needs a CCTV camera. We have CCTV cameras. Just one is fine.

2132
01:41:52,590 --> 01:41:59,950
CCTV camera, just one — oh it dropped, I dropped it. Wait, it needs pipes too.

2133
01:41:59,950 --> 01:42:04,810
Do we still have pipes? We used all the pipes.

2134
01:42:05,430 --> 01:42:07,230
We're done for!

2135
01:42:07,230 --> 01:42:09,230
We can't load the missiles without them.

2136
01:42:09,230 --> 01:42:11,030
There are 13 in the trash can!

2137
01:42:11,030 --> 01:42:12,830
Grab the CCTV over there.

2138
01:42:12,830 --> 01:42:14,830
There are 13 pipes in the trash can.

2139
01:42:14,830 --> 01:42:16,590
What?!

2140
01:42:16,590 --> 01:42:18,430
The CCTV—

2141
01:42:18,430 --> 01:42:20,430
It's right here! This, this, this!

2142
01:42:20,430 --> 01:42:22,230
At your feet.

2143
01:42:22,230 --> 01:42:24,230
It's at your feet.

2144
01:42:24,230 --> 01:42:26,030
There are 13 pipes in the trash can.

2145
01:42:26,030 --> 01:42:28,030
13 pipes, bam bam bam!

2146
01:42:28,030 --> 01:42:29,870
There are 13 pipes, bam bam bam!

2147
01:42:29,870 --> 01:42:31,830
Where's the heli now?

2148
01:42:31,830 --> 01:42:33,630
With this—

2149
01:42:33,630 --> 01:42:35,430
Has it moved further away?

2150
01:42:35,430 --> 01:42:37,230
Let's lure the heli over.

2151
01:42:37,230 --> 01:42:39,030
Hey, heli!

2152
01:42:39,030 --> 01:42:40,830
Heli!

2153
01:42:40,830 --> 01:42:42,830
The heli will come, right?

2154
01:42:42,830 --> 01:42:44,630
It's an NPC.

2155
01:42:44,630 --> 01:42:46,230
Obviously.

2156
01:42:46,230 --> 01:42:48,030
Obviously.

2157
01:42:48,030 --> 01:42:49,830
The house will get destroyed.

2158
01:42:49,830 --> 01:42:53,630
We don't want the heli destroying the house.

2159
01:42:53,630 --> 01:42:55,330
Exactly.

2160
01:42:55,330 --> 01:42:57,230
Let's go fight the NPCs.

2161
01:42:57,230 --> 01:42:59,030
This...

2162
01:42:59,030 --> 01:43:02,490
Oh wait, CCTV...

2163
01:43:02,490 --> 01:43:04,490
I can only make one CCTV

2164
01:43:04,490 --> 01:43:12,400
Did we get it?!

2165
01:43:12,400 --> 01:43:17,810
Huh? I can't get any more

2166
01:43:17,810 --> 01:43:18,810
That's the worst

2167
01:43:18,810 --> 01:43:20,610
CC...

2168
01:43:20,610 --> 01:43:23,650
TV...

2169
01:43:23,650 --> 01:43:25,450
Gabun!

2170
01:43:25,450 --> 01:43:28,050
I thought we actually got it!

2171
01:43:29,050 --> 01:43:32,820
What are you doing?

2172
01:43:32,820 --> 01:43:34,620
I was messing around with the NPCs

2173
01:43:34,620 --> 01:43:36,420
Ah, I see

2174
01:43:36,420 --> 01:43:38,220
That one's hopeless

2175
01:43:38,220 --> 01:43:40,220
Polka...

2176
01:43:40,220 --> 01:43:44,020
Did you get taken out? You okay?

2177
01:43:44,020 --> 01:43:46,020
Yeah, I totally got taken out

2178
01:43:46,020 --> 01:43:47,820
Polka just keeps dying, huh

2179
01:43:47,820 --> 01:43:49,820
Because I'm weak

2180
01:43:49,820 --> 01:43:53,620
Why though?

2181
01:43:53,620 --> 01:43:55,420
Hey, the heli got away!

2182
01:43:55,420 --> 01:43:57,220
Come here!

2183
01:43:57,220 --> 01:43:57,720
Come here!

2184
01:43:57,720 --> 01:43:58,480
Do you have anything?

2185
01:43:58,480 --> 01:44:03,780
No cameras

2186
01:44:03,780 --> 01:44:07,630
You need a camera?

2187
01:44:07,630 --> 01:44:09,590
Is the CCTV camera a physical item?

2188
01:44:09,590 --> 01:44:12,730
I only had the one I gave you

2189
01:44:12,730 --> 01:44:14,030
How many did you need?

2190
01:44:14,030 --> 01:44:19,470
I need one to make a homing missile

2191
01:44:19,470 --> 01:44:22,070
Wasn't the one I gave you enough?

2192
01:44:22,070 --> 01:44:25,250
I can make one, but not two

2193
01:44:27,010 --> 01:44:29,250
But we each have one now, thanks

2194
01:44:29,250 --> 01:44:32,030
Um...

2195
01:44:32,030 --> 01:44:33,670
I used one to research it

2196
01:44:33,670 --> 01:44:35,310
Ah, that's why

2197
01:44:35,310 --> 01:44:36,890
So there's only one left

2198
01:44:36,890 --> 01:44:38,590
Then let's fight with one

2199
01:44:38,590 --> 01:44:41,270
Let's do it together then

2200
01:44:41,270 --> 01:44:42,530
Yeah, let's

2201
01:44:42,530 --> 01:44:43,170
Yeah...

2202
01:44:43,170 --> 01:44:44,230
Yeah

2203
01:44:44,230 --> 01:44:46,670
Yeah

2204
01:44:46,670 --> 01:44:49,630
There are still NPCs here

2205
01:44:49,630 --> 01:44:51,550
Watch out for them

2206
01:44:51,550 --> 01:44:55,240
Where are the NPCs?

2207
01:44:55,440 --> 01:44:57,380
Straight ahead

2208
01:44:57,380 --> 01:45:00,700
I'm not shooting yet

2209
01:45:00,700 --> 01:45:02,500
Huh? Genius?

2210
01:45:02,500 --> 01:45:08,880
There's just one

2211
01:45:08,880 --> 01:45:11,680
A homing missile

2212
01:45:11,680 --> 01:45:16,870
But the heli went somewhere

2213
01:45:16,870 --> 01:45:20,230
Let's just get ready for it

2214
01:45:20,230 --> 01:45:23,030
Oh, if I'm not shooting I'll use the M249

2215
01:45:23,030 --> 01:45:24,030
Okay okay okay

2216
01:45:24,030 --> 01:45:25,830
Get behind—

2217
01:45:25,830 --> 01:45:26,780
Huh?

2218
01:45:27,630 --> 01:45:28,810
Polka's shooting?

2219
01:45:28,810 --> 01:45:30,510
Yeah, you handle the homing missile

2220
01:45:30,510 --> 01:45:33,810
It didn't even hit at this close range

2221
01:45:33,810 --> 01:45:35,390
Polka's shooting?

2222
01:45:35,390 --> 01:45:39,190
It's homing, so it should track the target

2223
01:45:39,190 --> 01:45:41,490
Really?

2224
01:45:41,490 --> 01:45:43,190
Otherwise why would they call it homing?

2225
01:45:43,190 --> 01:45:46,570
Can I get some ammo?

2226
01:45:46,570 --> 01:45:52,200
Oh I had ammo

2227
01:45:52,200 --> 01:45:55,760
Not that way, not that way!

2228
01:45:55,760 --> 01:45:57,640
Is it coming? Did it come?

2229
01:45:57,700 --> 01:46:01,850
That pretty face of yours—

2230
01:46:01,850 --> 01:46:05,980
Oh wait, the M249 is this one

2231
01:46:05,980 --> 01:46:08,040
Whoa, this is crazy, what is this

2232
01:46:08,040 --> 01:46:10,260
I want to get eyes on it first

2233
01:46:10,260 --> 01:46:17,160
Let's move away from the base

2234
01:46:17,160 --> 01:46:17,760
Right

2235
01:46:17,760 --> 01:46:20,740
So Nikotan doesn't get caught in the crossfire

2236
01:46:20,740 --> 01:46:22,360
Where?

2237
01:46:22,360 --> 01:46:23,940
There's a horse over there

2238
01:46:23,940 --> 01:46:24,700
Where?

2239
01:46:24,700 --> 01:46:27,770
Where is it?

2240
01:46:27,770 --> 01:46:29,830
Why is it always like this

2241
01:46:29,830 --> 01:46:30,830
Oh, there it is!

2242
01:46:30,830 --> 01:46:32,630
It's pretty far away

2243
01:46:32,630 --> 01:46:34,430
Yeah, really far

2244
01:46:34,430 --> 01:46:37,230
I'd rather it be a bit closer

2245
01:46:37,230 --> 01:46:40,030
How do you lock on? Lock on?

2246
01:46:40,030 --> 01:46:42,830
Maybe you can lock on if you get closer?

2247
01:46:42,830 --> 01:46:44,630
Oh, you're right

2248
01:46:44,630 --> 01:46:46,430
It says "Lock"

2249
01:46:46,430 --> 01:46:48,230
Oh, I see

2250
01:46:48,230 --> 01:46:50,230
Why does it never show up when you need it, seriously

2251
01:46:50,230 --> 01:46:53,030
Shoot that thing, Kanata!

2252
01:46:53,030 --> 01:46:55,830
Can't see it

2253
01:46:55,830 --> 01:46:57,830
It's really far

2254
01:46:57,830 --> 01:47:00,330
The Minicopter's gone off somewhere

2255
01:47:00,330 --> 01:47:05,770
J, I, 16? Are you kidding me

2256
01:47:05,770 --> 01:47:09,170
Why?! Why?!

2257
01:47:09,170 --> 01:47:11,890
It was chasing us so hard just a moment ago

2258
01:47:11,890 --> 01:47:14,110
Did it sense danger?

2259
01:47:14,110 --> 01:47:18,880
So it can sense danger too, huh

2260
01:47:18,880 --> 01:47:24,290
Did it figure out we have homing missiles?

2261
01:47:24,290 --> 01:47:27,830
It knows us way too well

2262
01:47:27,830 --> 01:47:29,610
It went completely the other way

2263
01:47:29,610 --> 01:47:30,390
It's just gonna go home like this

2264
01:47:30,390 --> 01:47:31,530
Oh, it suddenly came back

2265
01:47:31,530 --> 01:47:33,370
Is it coming?

2266
01:47:33,370 --> 01:47:36,870
Direction-wise it feels like it might come this way

2267
01:47:36,870 --> 01:47:38,870
Laser

2268
01:47:38,870 --> 01:47:45,260
Hey, seriously stop ghosting us, helicopter

2269
01:47:45,260 --> 01:47:47,120
You can scope too

2270
01:47:47,120 --> 01:47:50,040
Wow, you can hear it from that far away?

2271
01:47:50,040 --> 01:47:58,190
It's heading toward Water Treatment

2272
01:48:01,980 --> 01:48:05,520
Where'd the heli go?

2273
01:48:05,520 --> 01:48:07,760
Right now it's at G13

2274
01:48:07,760 --> 01:48:10,000
That's really far

2275
01:48:10,000 --> 01:48:11,860
What's going on?

2276
01:48:11,860 --> 01:48:13,440
It's not coming over here

2277
01:48:13,440 --> 01:48:14,040
What's up?

2278
01:48:14,040 --> 01:48:16,060
It's scared

2279
01:48:16,060 --> 01:48:18,840
It's scared of us

2280
01:48:18,840 --> 01:48:24,920
It suddenly got scared

2281
01:48:24,920 --> 01:48:30,930
Good angle of approach

2282
01:48:30,930 --> 01:48:31,890
More showed up

2283
01:48:31,890 --> 01:48:40,740
Niko off-stream might get spooked again

2284
01:48:42,130 --> 01:48:45,430
The heli sound...

2285
01:48:45,430 --> 01:48:48,230
It's getting closer!

2286
01:48:48,230 --> 01:48:51,180
Oh but it's kind of...

2287
01:48:51,180 --> 01:48:52,180
It's heading toward the dome

2288
01:48:52,180 --> 01:48:55,980
How close do we need to be for it to work?

2289
01:48:55,980 --> 01:48:59,780
It's flying but you probably have to be in roughly the same grid square

2290
01:48:59,780 --> 01:49:01,780
What?!

2291
01:49:01,780 --> 01:49:03,580
That's super close!

2292
01:49:03,580 --> 01:49:04,580
Bathroom

2293
01:49:04,580 --> 01:49:06,320
Did you shoot just now, Kanata?

2294
01:49:06,320 --> 01:49:08,180
I took a shot but — bathroom

2295
01:49:08,180 --> 01:49:18,050
It's a bit far

2296
01:49:18,050 --> 01:49:21,050
Now I'm gonna chase you, heli!

2297
01:49:21,050 --> 01:49:24,850
Now it's your turn to be chased — brace yourself

2298
01:49:24,850 --> 01:49:30,210
The lock-on is powerful though

2299
01:49:30,210 --> 01:49:33,010
I wanna see it fire the missile

2300
01:49:33,010 --> 01:49:36,270
This might actually work

2301
01:49:36,270 --> 01:49:39,570
Patrol Helicopter

2302
01:49:39,570 --> 01:49:42,210
That thing is...

2303
01:49:42,210 --> 01:49:45,110
Where'd it go?

2304
01:49:45,110 --> 01:49:50,550
It went off toward the sea on the right

2305
01:49:50,550 --> 01:49:55,150
Oh, all the cars are gone now

2306
01:49:55,150 --> 01:50:01,570
Right? For real — I was a little shocked when I saw the car was beyond repair

2307
01:50:01,590 --> 01:50:04,170
Yeah, I thought it just couldn't be fixed

2308
01:50:04,170 --> 01:50:05,930
We got wrecked

2309
01:50:05,930 --> 01:50:09,910
Wait, Polka's not even showing up on the map anymore

2310
01:50:09,910 --> 01:50:11,430
That thing...

2311
01:50:11,430 --> 01:50:13,330
Is it retreating?

2312
01:50:13,330 --> 01:50:15,230
Did it lose? Is that what happened?

2313
01:50:15,230 --> 01:50:16,010
Wow

2314
01:50:16,010 --> 01:50:16,610
It's admitting defeat...

2315
01:50:16,610 --> 01:50:18,510
Yeah, it stopped coming

2316
01:50:18,510 --> 01:50:21,390


2317
01:50:21,390 --> 01:50:22,610


2318
01:50:22,610 --> 01:50:24,150
There's still a bicycle though

2319
01:50:24,150 --> 01:50:26,110


2320
01:50:26,110 --> 01:50:27,250
Yeah, at this point the bike is literally all we have left

2321
01:50:27,250 --> 01:50:28,230
A bike and a horse.

2322
01:50:28,230 --> 01:50:31,310
When you think about it, the bike is literally all we've got.

2323
01:50:31,310 --> 01:50:34,950
Wait, there's actually a way to fully repair it, right?

2324
01:50:34,950 --> 01:50:36,510
Like, technically.

2325
01:50:36,510 --> 01:50:37,970
If you just bang on it—

2326
01:50:37,970 --> 01:50:39,150
That should fix it, right?

2327
01:50:39,150 --> 01:50:41,250
Uh, well... hmm, I wonder...

2328
01:50:41,250 --> 01:50:43,470
Oh, nope, it's not fixing. It's completely broken now.

2329
01:50:43,470 --> 01:50:45,710
Yeah, the frame itself is busted, so

2330
01:50:45,710 --> 01:50:47,090
we'll have to find another one somewhere.

2331
01:50:47,090 --> 01:50:50,580
Oh, this one's done for too, it's broken.

2332
01:50:50,580 --> 01:50:57,930
It might've still been okay a little while ago.

2333
01:50:57,930 --> 01:50:59,860
Welp, that's the end of that.

2334
01:50:59,860 --> 01:51:01,410
It's gone.

2335
01:51:01,410 --> 01:51:03,410
If we're doing a night run, it's gotta be the heli.

2336
01:51:03,410 --> 01:51:05,250
Yeah.

2337
01:51:05,250 --> 01:51:09,150
For a night run, definitely the heli.

2338
01:51:09,150 --> 01:51:10,490
By the way,

2339
01:51:10,490 --> 01:51:12,910
can you craft homing missiles?

2340
01:51:12,910 --> 01:51:16,670
Hmm, good question.

2341
01:51:16,670 --> 01:51:19,370
Let me check real quick—

2342
01:51:19,370 --> 01:51:21,270
can I research them?

2343
01:51:21,270 --> 01:51:24,830
In the end we only have like 9 homing missiles anyway.

2344
01:51:28,170 --> 01:51:29,980
Only 9?

2345
01:51:29,980 --> 01:51:31,970
Yeah, not even 9.

2346
01:51:31,970 --> 01:51:37,680
Can't craft this item from scrap.

2347
01:51:37,680 --> 01:51:44,610
Even though it's a homing missile?

2348
01:51:44,610 --> 01:51:48,590
Do we have to craft it somewhere specific?

2349
01:51:48,590 --> 01:51:50,540
Is this a missile?

2350
01:51:50,540 --> 01:51:53,740
Which one's the homing one?

2351
01:51:53,740 --> 01:51:55,740
The one called Homing Missile.

2352
01:51:55,740 --> 01:51:57,740
There's a Homing Missile Launcher, right?

2353
01:51:57,740 --> 01:51:59,540
The one that needs a surveillance camera?

2354
01:51:59,540 --> 01:52:01,720
This one, yeah, exactly.

2355
01:52:01,720 --> 01:52:04,960
Let's see, can I research the ammo for this?

2356
01:52:04,960 --> 01:52:10,950
Oh, it's already researched. I can craft it.

2357
01:52:10,950 --> 01:52:12,410
Oh nice, it's already unlocked. Good job.

2358
01:52:12,410 --> 01:52:14,330
So should we craft a bunch of them?

2359
01:52:14,330 --> 01:52:16,050
Well, I mean...

2360
01:52:16,050 --> 01:52:21,380
We've really spent everything we had, huh.

2361
01:52:21,380 --> 01:52:23,980
Yeah, gotta use it all today.

2362
01:52:23,980 --> 01:52:25,540
For real?

2363
01:52:25,540 --> 01:52:27,860
Pipes... we're using pipes again?

2364
01:52:27,860 --> 01:52:29,700
Pipes, gunpowder, junk...

2365
01:52:30,140 --> 01:52:35,100
We're running low on pipes too. Hurry up with the junk.

2366
01:52:35,100 --> 01:52:38,940
I'll craft some homing missiles.

2367
01:52:38,940 --> 01:52:41,900
Homing missiles.

2368
01:52:41,900 --> 01:52:44,610
They say 9 is enough, but still.

2369
01:52:44,610 --> 01:52:47,580
I actually want to craft the launcher itself.

2370
01:52:47,580 --> 01:52:54,450
Yeah, the launcher — we need Botan's CCTV camera for that. Really want that launcher.

2371
01:52:54,450 --> 01:52:57,450
Gotta find a camera first. Yep.

2372
01:52:58,250 --> 01:53:00,050
Can we get to the beach?

2373
01:53:00,050 --> 01:53:05,050
The fact that we're already at the point of crafting a launcher is honestly terrifying.

2374
01:53:05,050 --> 01:53:08,350
Right?

2375
01:53:08,350 --> 01:53:11,250
It's a CCTV launcher, so we definitely need one.

2376
01:53:11,250 --> 01:53:15,350
I never even thought about crafting a launcher before, even now.

2377
01:53:15,350 --> 01:53:19,750
I wonder if there's one around...

2378
01:53:19,750 --> 01:53:27,650
Hmm, this is a hatch, right?

2379
01:53:28,450 --> 01:53:32,450
What should we do about Nene's place — we tidied it up already.

2380
01:53:32,450 --> 01:53:38,000
Oh, maybe the shop sells one.

2381
01:53:38,000 --> 01:53:40,650
CCTV...

2382
01:53:40,650 --> 01:53:43,650
I wonder what the most expensive thing in the shop is.

2383
01:53:43,650 --> 01:53:47,980
Probably the heli or something, right?

2384
01:53:47,980 --> 01:53:48,860
The heli, huh.

2385
01:53:48,860 --> 01:53:49,780
The large heli...

2386
01:53:49,780 --> 01:53:50,780
CCTV camera.

2387
01:53:58,870 --> 01:54:03,410
Riding the large heli.

2388
01:54:03,410 --> 01:54:08,440
I hope they have one...

2389
01:54:08,440 --> 01:54:12,620
Do we have to go all the way to Bandit Camp?

2390
01:54:12,620 --> 01:54:16,630
Well, we do have a heli though.

2391
01:54:16,630 --> 01:54:18,570
We have a heli, but...

2392
01:54:18,570 --> 01:54:21,030
We've got the heli.

2393
01:54:21,030 --> 01:54:22,570
We've got the heli.

2394
01:54:22,570 --> 01:54:26,070
No CCTV camera.

2395
01:54:26,070 --> 01:54:28,530
Nope, they don't sell it.

2396
01:54:30,470 --> 01:54:37,510
Hey Naatan, what do you think about the heli? Landing is pretty tricky though.

2397
01:54:37,510 --> 01:54:40,670
If we take the heli it'll be super fast.

2398
01:54:40,670 --> 01:54:45,550
True, but I kinda don't want to ride it...

2399
01:54:45,550 --> 01:54:55,550
It'd be instant by heli, so why not? Our options are bike, horse, or heli at this point.

2400
01:54:56,140 --> 01:55:00,640
Just take the heli, it's easy.

2401
01:55:01,260 --> 01:55:03,260
Uh oh, the landing is rough!

2402
01:55:03,260 --> 01:55:05,940
Polka doesn't know how to fly it!

2403
01:55:05,940 --> 01:55:09,100
Why don't you try riding it, Polka?

2404
01:55:09,100 --> 01:55:11,100
I'll wreck it instantly, just so you know.

2405
01:55:11,100 --> 01:55:13,880
It's fine, we have scrap, 5000 yen worth.

2406
01:55:13,880 --> 01:55:18,320
Great, then you can repair it, Luna.

2407
01:55:18,320 --> 01:55:22,700
Repair it a ton, and we'll ride it in the morning.

2408
01:55:22,700 --> 01:55:25,320
It's the feel of it, the riding sensation...

2409
01:55:25,320 --> 01:55:27,320
Yeah, repair it, repair it.

2410
01:55:29,800 --> 01:55:32,400
It needs a bit of fuel though.

2411
01:55:32,400 --> 01:55:37,860
Hmm...

2412
01:55:37,860 --> 01:55:40,580
I don't really need this, but I'll put it in here anyway.

2413
01:55:40,580 --> 01:55:48,040
The heli stopped coming.

2414
01:55:48,040 --> 01:55:49,600
The heli already left.

2415
01:55:49,600 --> 01:55:53,940
We'll wait until it announces it's spawned again before going after it.

2416
01:55:53,940 --> 01:55:55,640
Why does the heli always...

2417
01:55:55,640 --> 01:55:57,780
It was so sudden, wasn't it?

2418
01:55:57,780 --> 01:56:02,380
The moment we said we were gonna go for it, it turned around and left.

2419
01:56:03,640 --> 01:56:05,080
I hate that about it.

2420
01:56:05,080 --> 01:56:06,240
Seriously though.

2421
01:56:06,240 --> 01:56:06,640
Right?

2422
01:56:06,640 --> 01:56:09,440
It's totally playing us.

2423
01:56:09,440 --> 01:56:18,320
Well, we could always build a car from scratch.

2424
01:56:18,320 --> 01:56:22,280
That was wild.

2425
01:56:22,280 --> 01:56:26,300
Hmm...

2426
01:56:26,300 --> 01:56:31,550
Wanna take the minicopter?

2427
01:56:31,550 --> 01:56:33,790
Aren't we taking the minicopter?

2428
01:56:33,790 --> 01:56:35,530
Where are we going?

2429
01:56:36,930 --> 01:56:38,990
I'm not sure if we can make it, but...

2430
01:56:38,990 --> 01:56:40,450
If we're riding it...

2431
01:56:40,450 --> 01:56:41,370
Where was it again?

2432
01:56:41,370 --> 01:56:43,870
If we're going...

2433
01:56:43,870 --> 01:56:45,870
What was it again?

2434
01:56:45,870 --> 01:56:46,770
This is scary.

2435
01:56:46,770 --> 01:56:50,840
It's the gambling one, right?

2436
01:56:50,840 --> 01:56:52,760
I'm going shopping.

2437
01:56:52,760 --> 01:56:56,660
This angle is a bit tricky.

2438
01:56:56,660 --> 01:56:59,760
There's a chance we could fall, you know.

2439
01:56:59,760 --> 01:57:02,720
Oh, Kanatan's going to clean up?

2440
01:57:02,720 --> 01:57:04,160
Oh, think you can do a popo?

2441
01:57:04,160 --> 01:57:05,420
Yeah, I can't do it.

2442
01:57:05,420 --> 01:57:07,780
So I was wondering what you'd do.

2443
01:57:07,780 --> 01:57:12,850
Well, it's worth a try.

2444
01:57:12,850 --> 01:57:14,550
Even though I can't do it.

2445
01:57:14,550 --> 01:57:16,650
Shouldn't you not bring the M249?

2446
01:57:16,650 --> 01:57:19,250
Yeah.

2447
01:57:19,250 --> 01:57:21,150
Leave it at home?

2448
01:57:21,150 --> 01:57:22,890
Oh, think it'll fall?

2449
01:57:22,890 --> 01:57:25,710
Yeah.

2450
01:57:25,710 --> 01:57:31,910
Okay.

2451
01:57:31,910 --> 01:57:35,810
Just getting it out is hard enough.

2452
01:57:35,810 --> 01:57:37,230
Push push push.

2453
01:57:37,230 --> 01:57:38,990
Push push push push.

2454
01:57:38,990 --> 01:57:42,090
And then a little bit with the controller while riding.

2455
01:57:42,090 --> 01:57:44,150
Ooh~

2456
01:57:44,150 --> 01:57:47,880
Do I hold onto it?

2457
01:57:47,880 --> 01:57:51,450
Oh, there was no fuel in it.

2458
01:57:51,450 --> 01:57:55,210
Put in fuel and then ride it.

2459
01:57:55,210 --> 01:57:57,250
Oh?

2460
01:57:57,250 --> 01:58:01,540
With the controller.

2461
01:58:01,540 --> 01:58:04,860
Oh!

2462
01:58:04,860 --> 01:58:06,100


2463
01:58:06,100 --> 01:58:08,000
Ooh!

2464
01:58:08,300 --> 01:58:10,300


2465
01:58:10,300 --> 01:58:12,950
I can see an airdrop.

2466
01:58:13,300 --> 01:58:14,300
Okay.

2467
01:58:14,300 --> 01:58:16,300
What?

2468
01:58:16,300 --> 01:58:17,300
Don't just say okay.

2469
01:58:17,300 --> 01:58:20,300
To fly, uh, it's W.

2470
01:58:20,300 --> 01:58:22,300
Which way does this go up again?

2471
01:58:22,300 --> 01:58:25,300
Hold W to go up?

2472
01:58:25,300 --> 01:58:29,300
Wait, does that mean I can crash it? Are you telling me to drive?

2473
01:58:29,300 --> 01:58:31,300
So you're driving then!

2474
01:58:31,300 --> 01:58:33,300
Let's go!

2475
01:58:33,300 --> 01:58:36,020
I've been waiting for this!

2476
01:58:35,810 --> 01:58:38,910
Wait, I thought I left the M249 behind but I still have it.

2477
01:58:38,910 --> 01:58:43,440
Let Amane-chan hold it.

2478
01:58:43,440 --> 01:58:44,760
No wait.

2479
01:58:44,760 --> 01:58:47,080
Oh, I put down the wrong thing?

2480
01:58:47,080 --> 01:58:48,880
Let Amane-chan hold it.

2481
01:58:48,880 --> 01:58:49,760
M249

2482
01:58:49,760 --> 01:58:53,080
This is the M249

2483
01:58:53,080 --> 01:58:53,420
Alright

2484
01:58:53,420 --> 01:58:57,580
Here we go

2485
01:58:57,580 --> 01:59:00,820
Hah

2486
01:59:00,820 --> 01:59:02,320
Okay then

2487
01:59:02,320 --> 01:59:05,660
Is it here?

2488
01:59:05,660 --> 01:59:07,420
Hmm, let's see...

2489
01:59:07,420 --> 01:59:10,160
The casino... the gambling den...

2490
01:59:10,160 --> 01:59:10,960
Roughly...

2491
01:59:10,960 --> 01:59:12,660
Wait, I forgot how to do this

2492
01:59:12,660 --> 01:59:13,960
Isn't it supposed to go straight?

2493
01:59:13,960 --> 01:59:16,520
Where's the gambling den?

2494
01:59:16,520 --> 01:59:19,980
One-day camp

2495
01:59:19,980 --> 01:59:22,440
Oh, hold on

2496
01:59:22,440 --> 01:59:23,640
What the—!?

2497
01:59:23,640 --> 01:59:29,080
The wings... the wings hit something

2498
01:59:29,080 --> 01:59:30,900
Roughly heading... heading north

2499
01:59:30,900 --> 01:59:33,240
Oh! Nice! That's great!

2500
01:59:33,240 --> 01:59:37,400
Wow, you're so good at this, Hime!

2501
01:59:37,400 --> 01:59:39,320
I can only go up though

2502
01:59:39,320 --> 01:59:41,720
Going up is important! But keep it straight

2503
01:59:41,720 --> 01:59:43,380
Wonderful!

2504
01:59:43,380 --> 01:59:44,700
The angle looks good too

2505
01:59:44,700 --> 01:59:46,340
Keep it level, keep it level

2506
01:59:46,340 --> 01:59:47,480
Oh, you're going backwards?

2507
01:59:47,480 --> 01:59:48,400
You're going backwards, Hime

2508
01:59:48,400 --> 01:59:51,720
You need to go forward, lean forward

2509
01:59:51,720 --> 01:59:53,500
I can do the indicator poles, you know

2510
01:59:53,500 --> 01:59:56,160
Hmm, okay

2511
01:59:56,160 --> 01:59:58,200
You're doing great, Hime

2512
01:59:58,200 --> 02:00:01,660
Phew

2513
02:00:01,660 --> 02:00:05,890
I can see the airdrop clearly

2514
02:00:06,390 --> 02:00:09,390
Flying feels good~ but landing is scary~

2515
02:00:09,390 --> 02:00:10,630
Landing is scary?

2516
02:00:10,630 --> 02:00:16,170
Well, with planes and stuff, takeoff and landing are the most dangerous

2517
02:00:16,170 --> 02:00:18,490
That's so true~

2518
02:00:18,490 --> 02:00:20,630
But hey~

2519
02:00:20,630 --> 02:00:21,850
Aren't you doing well?

2520
02:00:21,850 --> 02:00:24,070
Really~?

2521
02:00:24,070 --> 02:00:24,830
Yeah

2522
02:00:24,830 --> 02:00:26,150
Wait, wha—?

2523
02:00:26,150 --> 02:00:30,050
Where did you learn this? Isn't this amazing?

2524
02:00:30,050 --> 02:00:31,630
Self-taught

2525
02:00:31,630 --> 02:00:33,930
Isn't that incredible? Aren't you good at this? Whoa!?

2526
02:00:34,790 --> 02:00:38,820
But

2527
02:00:38,820 --> 02:00:40,620
Where is it?

2528
02:00:40,620 --> 02:00:44,130
We're getting closer

2529
02:00:44,130 --> 02:00:46,130
Where should I land?

2530
02:00:46,130 --> 02:00:47,930
Where's the safe zone?

2531
02:00:47,930 --> 02:00:49,930
Won't we get shot down by the patrol helicopter?

2532
02:00:49,930 --> 02:00:51,730
Apparently we won't get shot down here

2533
02:00:51,730 --> 02:00:53,730
Oh, okay then

2534
02:00:53,730 --> 02:00:55,620
Something like this should be fine, right?

2535
02:00:55,620 --> 02:00:57,530
Oh, we're getting closer and closer

2536
02:00:57,530 --> 02:01:01,130
Oh nice, nice!

2537
02:01:01,130 --> 02:01:05,130
So good, so good, so good!

2538
02:01:07,050 --> 02:01:08,850
Ow— oh, huh?

2539
02:01:08,850 --> 02:01:10,650
It broke

2540
02:01:10,650 --> 02:01:12,650
Ow

2541
02:01:12,650 --> 02:01:15,650
It's fine, we can fix this, no problem

2542
02:01:15,650 --> 02:01:17,450
Did we hit a rock or something?

2543
02:01:17,450 --> 02:01:19,250
Yeah, this rock is to blame

2544
02:01:19,250 --> 02:01:20,250
The rock is at fault

2545
02:01:20,250 --> 02:01:22,250
It shouldn't even be there, it shouldn't be there

2546
02:01:22,250 --> 02:01:25,050
You did great, you did great!

2547
02:01:25,050 --> 02:01:26,050
Huh?

2548
02:01:26,050 --> 02:01:27,050
It kind of broke, but are you okay?

2549
02:01:27,050 --> 02:01:29,050
Wasn't that good though? Seriously

2550
02:01:29,050 --> 02:01:29,850
It's fine, it's fine

2551
02:01:29,850 --> 02:01:31,850
That was, you know, one of those...

2552
02:01:31,850 --> 02:01:33,450
What do you call it?

2553
02:01:33,450 --> 02:01:35,250
A performance

2554
02:01:35,250 --> 02:01:38,250
That was a performance, see? It's totally clean, right?

2555
02:01:38,250 --> 02:01:39,250
It's sitting on a rock though.

2556
02:01:39,250 --> 02:01:42,870
Oh, it's fine, it fixed itself.

2557
02:01:42,870 --> 02:01:43,870
Whoa!

2558
02:01:43,870 --> 02:01:46,670
Oh, somehow it worked out.

2559
02:01:46,670 --> 02:01:49,270
"Somehow it worked out," she says.

2560
02:01:49,270 --> 02:01:54,070
You've grown so much at so many things! Hime!

2561
02:01:54,070 --> 02:01:59,670
Man, this Rust session had so many things going on.

2562
02:01:59,670 --> 02:02:01,670
It's basically Hime's story of growth!

2563
02:02:03,470 --> 02:02:10,410
Do you have any CCTV cameras? You said they weren't sold here.

2564
02:02:10,410 --> 02:02:12,720
You don't have any? You said they weren't sold here.

2565
02:02:12,720 --> 02:02:18,100
Can't buy what they don't have. Do you sell them?

2566
02:02:18,100 --> 02:02:23,880
Guess not. You can't buy what they don't sell.

2567
02:02:23,880 --> 02:02:28,980
Nothing here. Wait, why did we come again?

2568
02:02:28,980 --> 02:02:31,360
To see if they sell CCTV cameras.

2569
02:02:31,360 --> 02:02:33,640
They probably don't, right?

2570
02:02:33,640 --> 02:02:35,440
Maybe I missed it.

2571
02:02:35,440 --> 02:02:37,080
There might be something here.

2572
02:02:37,080 --> 02:02:40,220
There's nobody around.

2573
02:02:40,220 --> 02:02:43,460
I've just never bought a CCTV camera before, so I don't even know where to look.

2574
02:02:43,460 --> 02:02:46,200
Yeah.

2575
02:02:46,200 --> 02:02:48,920
Never had to buy one until now.

2576
02:02:48,920 --> 02:02:53,190
Nothing here.

2577
02:02:53,190 --> 02:02:54,410
Nothing here.

2578
02:02:54,410 --> 02:02:56,410
Maybe they just don't have it.

2579
02:02:56,410 --> 02:02:58,650
What about a mini-heli for Polka to practice with?

2580
02:02:59,270 --> 02:03:01,070
Oh!

2581
02:03:01,070 --> 02:03:03,870
Do you have money?

2582
02:03:03,870 --> 02:03:05,870
I brought 2800 scrap, so I can buy it.

2583
02:03:05,870 --> 02:03:07,670
Let's get it!

2584
02:03:07,670 --> 02:03:09,490
Pol-Pol, over here.

2585
02:03:09,490 --> 02:03:11,270
Air.

2586
02:03:11,270 --> 02:03:13,070
Wolf.

2587
02:03:13,070 --> 02:03:15,070
Whoa, that's nostalgic.

2588
02:03:15,070 --> 02:03:17,870
Those gunshots.

2589
02:03:17,870 --> 02:03:18,870
Eh, it's fine.

2590
02:03:18,870 --> 02:03:21,470
Same old, same old.

2591
02:03:21,470 --> 02:03:23,470
You can buy it here.

2592
02:03:23,470 --> 02:03:25,270
Pol-Pol, money.

2593
02:03:25,270 --> 02:03:27,070
You could buy it for me, you know.

2594
02:03:27,070 --> 02:03:30,870
Let's see... aircraft.

2595
02:03:30,870 --> 02:03:31,870
Is this the smallest heli?

2596
02:03:31,870 --> 02:03:32,870
Mini heli.

2597
02:03:32,870 --> 02:03:34,670
750.

2598
02:03:34,670 --> 02:03:36,270
Thank you.

2599
02:03:36,270 --> 02:03:38,270
The rideable heli is way too scary, right?

2600
02:03:38,270 --> 02:03:39,270
Yeah.

2601
02:03:39,270 --> 02:03:40,070
Here's your change.

2602
02:03:40,070 --> 02:03:40,870
It's terrifying.

2603
02:03:40,870 --> 02:03:41,870
Oh!

2604
02:03:41,870 --> 02:03:44,670
Give me some tips!

2605
02:03:44,670 --> 02:03:48,470
So, you want to move the mouse really slowly.

2606
02:03:48,470 --> 02:03:51,270
Wait, how do I even make it go up?

2607
02:03:51,270 --> 02:03:53,270
Press W to start the engine.

2608
02:03:53,270 --> 02:03:56,090
Hold W to go up.

2609
02:03:56,090 --> 02:03:58,090
S to go down.

2610
02:03:58,090 --> 02:04:00,810
And to change direction—

2611
02:04:00,810 --> 02:04:02,810
Use A or D to turn.

2612
02:04:02,810 --> 02:04:05,810
And use the mouse to keep it level.

2613
02:04:05,810 --> 02:04:07,810
If you tilt forward—

2614
02:04:07,810 --> 02:04:10,170
It goes forward.

2615
02:04:10,170 --> 02:04:10,790
Wait, no, that's not right.

2616
02:04:10,790 --> 02:04:13,290
Moving the mouse up tilts it forward.

2617
02:04:13,290 --> 02:04:14,470
Can you hear me? This thing.

2618
02:04:14,470 --> 02:04:15,410
I can hear you.

2619
02:04:15,410 --> 02:04:16,410
If you can't hear—

2620
02:04:16,410 --> 02:04:17,390
I can hear it.

2621
02:04:17,390 --> 02:04:19,690
You're going way up though.

2622
02:04:19,690 --> 02:04:21,870
I went up! What do I do now?!

2623
02:04:21,870 --> 02:04:25,390
To move forward—

2624
02:04:25,390 --> 02:04:28,250
Move the mouse slightly upward.

2625
02:04:28,250 --> 02:04:30,270
And you'll go forward.

2626
02:04:30,270 --> 02:04:31,730
When you're going backward—

2627
02:04:31,730 --> 02:04:32,990
Your mouse is going back—

2628
02:04:32,990 --> 02:04:35,290
Oh, you're moving the mouse down.

2629
02:04:35,290 --> 02:04:36,750
Move it up.

2630
02:04:36,750 --> 02:04:38,390
Move it up.

2631
02:04:38,390 --> 02:04:38,970
Huh?

2632
02:04:38,970 --> 02:04:41,930
What are you talking about?

2633
02:04:41,930 --> 02:04:46,370
Well, you just have to get a feel for it.

2634
02:04:48,130 --> 02:04:49,410
Tilt it a little.

2635
02:04:49,410 --> 02:04:51,410
Which direction is home?

2636
02:04:51,410 --> 02:04:54,410
This way?

2637
02:04:54,410 --> 02:04:57,520
But somehow—

2638
02:04:57,520 --> 02:04:58,980
You seem to be doing okay?

2639
02:04:58,980 --> 02:05:00,980
I'm going backward, I'm going backward!

2640
02:05:00,980 --> 02:05:02,700
What do I do when I'm going backward?

2641
02:05:02,700 --> 02:05:05,500
Move the mouse up, flick it upward—

2642
02:05:05,500 --> 02:05:07,300
if you flick it up, you'll go forward.

2643
02:05:07,300 --> 02:05:09,640
But I'm going backward when I flick it!

2644
02:05:09,640 --> 02:05:12,100
Mouse up! Up! UP!

2645
02:05:12,100 --> 02:05:13,900
When I say up—

2646
02:05:13,900 --> 02:05:16,100
Wait, I'm still going backward?

2647
02:05:16,900 --> 02:05:26,130
I keep turning it — you said up! Up, up, up — flick it up — huh? Up? Wait, going up makes me go backward?

2648
02:05:26,130 --> 02:05:29,900
Did I have it backwards? Did I say it wrong?

2649
02:05:29,900 --> 02:05:35,500
Oh, it's toward you — pull it toward you! Toward you? It was toward you!

2650
02:05:35,500 --> 02:05:44,220
Huh? But I'm still going backward. I can't figure it out unless I'm actually flying. Wait, was it backward?

2651
02:05:44,220 --> 02:05:47,560
Hold on — oh, too close, too close, too close! Wait — AHHH!

2652
02:05:47,560 --> 02:05:49,120
Too close — everything's too close — especially the ground!

2653
02:05:49,120 --> 02:05:50,860
Where did Popo go?

2654
02:05:50,860 --> 02:05:52,520
Oh — oh — she fell!

2655
02:05:52,520 --> 02:05:54,080
Popo fell, she fell!

2656
02:05:54,080 --> 02:05:55,320
Popo fell?

2657
02:05:55,320 --> 02:05:59,560
What happened?

2658
02:05:59,560 --> 02:06:03,200
Where even is this place?

2659
02:06:03,200 --> 02:06:06,300
How far did Popo fly?

2660
02:06:06,300 --> 02:06:09,600
Hmm, she flew pretty far — all the way over here.

2661
02:06:09,600 --> 02:06:11,060
She went all the way up north!

2662
02:06:11,060 --> 02:06:13,460
Popo's just not good at going forward.

2663
02:06:13,460 --> 02:06:15,260
How do you even go forward?

2664
02:06:15,260 --> 02:06:17,260
And she survived too!

2665
02:06:17,260 --> 02:06:22,060
I can't figure it out unless I'm actually doing it.

2666
02:06:22,060 --> 02:06:25,500
Going forward is just hard.

2667
02:06:25,500 --> 02:06:27,000
I keep going backward.

2668
02:06:27,000 --> 02:06:29,000
Wait, she's not dead? From that?

2669
02:06:29,000 --> 02:06:36,450
I thought I was getting pretty close to the ground there.

2670
02:06:36,450 --> 02:06:39,450
You probably hit Space and just died normally.

2671
02:06:39,450 --> 02:06:41,750
Oh, I see — I accidentally hit Space.

2672
02:06:41,750 --> 02:06:44,830
Oh, it's on fire — good thing I didn't crash into someone else's house.

2673
02:06:44,830 --> 02:06:48,200
Well, but still...

2674
02:06:48,200 --> 02:06:54,000
Like, the whole "push the mouse forward" thing—

2675
02:06:54,000 --> 02:06:56,020
I still don't really get it.

2676
02:06:56,020 --> 02:06:59,780
Does "forward" mean pulling it toward you, or...

2677
02:06:59,780 --> 02:07:01,340
pushing it away?

2678
02:07:01,340 --> 02:07:03,140
Is it pushing it away?

2679
02:07:03,140 --> 02:07:05,140
Oh wait, where did I put Shelly?

2680
02:07:05,140 --> 02:07:07,580
Oh, there it is.

2681
02:07:07,580 --> 02:07:13,190
Push it away? But even then it doesn't—

2682
02:07:13,510 --> 02:07:19,570
it doesn't work right. Maybe I'm not keeping it level.

2683
02:07:19,570 --> 02:07:24,680
W makes you go up.

2684
02:07:24,680 --> 02:07:34,540
Moving the mouse up should make you go forward.

2685
02:07:34,540 --> 02:07:42,860
Where's Popo?

2686
02:07:49,200 --> 02:07:53,780
Going backward is probably because the mouse is sliding down like this.

2687
02:07:53,780 --> 02:07:56,560
So I need to keep pushing it more and more forward?

2688
02:07:56,560 --> 02:08:05,840
Just a little is enough since it's fast.

2689
02:08:05,840 --> 02:08:10,540
I was trying to do just a little, but then somehow—

2690
02:08:10,540 --> 02:08:14,020
I just kept drifting further and further back.

2691
02:08:14,020 --> 02:08:16,140
Ugh, this is hard.

2692
02:08:16,140 --> 02:08:18,020
This is genuinely difficult.

2693
02:08:18,020 --> 02:08:21,720
It's really hard — Polka has never once gotten it right.

2694
02:08:21,730 --> 02:08:29,530
Wait, is someone coming to pick me up?

2695
02:08:33,200 --> 02:08:38,930
They came by helicopter!

2696
02:08:38,930 --> 02:08:40,930
Where is this?

2697
02:08:40,930 --> 02:08:44,730
Oh, here — it's that place.

2698
02:08:44,730 --> 02:08:46,670
Around here.

2699
02:08:46,670 --> 02:08:53,620
The people who are good at this are amazing.

2700
02:08:53,620 --> 02:08:56,120
